Just my thoughts, I think that the common baseline is an _extremely_ good reason to keep it in Java. Even in real-world greenfield projects, you would most likely stick to a language which your entire team is familiar with (be it Java, C++, Rust). 

I envision that it'll be really hard to perform reviews on each other's PRs if there wasn't a common language enforced, even if we limit to a subset of "common" languages.

You could also just do a project in your preferred language. Orbital, for example, would have given you the opportunity to play around with your preferred languages/frameworks, and I think it would be way easier for any kind of grading standards to be enforced with a common language.


