</div>

> > Tested on Linux (Ubuntu 24.04, x86_64), OpenJDK 25.0.4.
> > help works, mark/unmark are fine, tasks persist.
> > Main thing: both deadline and event are rejected unless a time is given. `deadline return book /by 2019-12-02` fails with "Invalid date inputted! Correct format: yyyy-MM-dd HHmm". A date with no time is a normal thing to enter, so consider defaulting the time instead of rejecting.
> > Minor: "Now you have 1 tasks in the list", and the empty todo error is a bare usage string while the other errors are friendlier.
