Doesn't seem to work on Linux. The cause is in the JAR itself. It bundles JavaFX 17.0.8, but the only native libraries inside are macOS x86_64 `.dylib` files:

```
libdecora_sse.dylib   libglass.dylib      libjavafx_font.dylib
libjavafx_iio.dylib   libprism_common.dylib
libprism_es2.dylib    libprism_sw.dylib
```

There are zero `.so` files (Linux) and zero `.dll` files (Windows). JavaFX tries the `es2` then `sw` pipeline, finds no loadable native for either, and aborts. This will fail the same way on any Windows machine.

To still review the app, I ran its classes against a stock OpenJFX 17.0.8 Linux SDK:

```
java -Dprism.order=sw --module-path javafx-sdk-17.0.8/lib \
     --add-modules javafx.controls,javafx.fxml \
     -cp <extracted griddel classes> jonathan.Launcher
```

Every command in the issue's test list worked. The application logic is fine, only the packaging is broken.

| Command | Result |
|---|---|
| `todo revise cs2103T` | Added |
| `deadline submit report /by 2026-09-20` | Added, rendered `Sep 20 2026` |
| `event project meeting /from 2026-09-20 /to 2026-09-21` | Added |
| `list` | All three, correct tags |
| `mark 1` / `unmark 1` | Toggles correctly |
| `find report` | Correct match |
| `check 2026-09-20` | Correctly returned both the deadline and the event on that date |
| `priority 1 high` / `2 medium` / `3 low` | All set, shown inline in `list` |
| `filter priority high` | Correct subset |
| `sort priority` | Correct high to low order |
| `list` after sort | Original order preserved, non-destructive, as documented |
| `delete 1` | Removed |
| `bye` | Window closes, exit code 0 |

One small bug, we can input dates that are such that the starting is later than the ending date. Might be worth fixing?

