Launches and works on Linux with a plain `java -jar linus.jar`. Every command in the user guide behaves as documented. One minor validation gap.

| Command | Result |
|---|---|
| `todo buy gifts` | Added, count correct |
| `deadline submit assignment /by 2026-01-01` | Added, date rendered `1 Jan 2026` as documented |
| `event attend exhibition /from 2026-01-01 /to 2026-01-02` | Added, both dates rendered |
| `list` | All three types, correct `[T]/[D]/[E]` tags |
| `mark 1` / `unmark 1` | `[X]` and `[ ]` toggle correctly |
| `find buy` | Matches only |
| `find exhibition` | Correctly showed `2.` Original list index preserved, matching the UG |
| `delete 1` | Removed, count updated |
| `bye` | Window closes, process exits with code 0 |

However, events accept an end date before the start date. `event trip /from 2026-02-02 /to 2026-01-01` is accepted and saved as
`[E][ ] trip (from: 2 Feb 2026 to: 1 Jan 2026)`. Probably worth rejecting, since every other bad input is caught. 

Also,  `find` with no matches prints an empty list. `find zzzz` replies "Here are the matching tasks in your list:" followed by
nothing. A "no matching tasks found" message would read better.

