**1. :fas-info-circle: Request to help with smoke testing JAR file**
</div>

* Link to JAR file: https://github.com/GeraldFSE/ip/releases/tag/v0.2
* Link to the User Guide: https://geraldfse.github.io/ip/
* Which OS'es to test on: Windows | Mac | Linux
* Things to check specifically:
  * Run from a terminal in an empty folder with `java -jar thomas.jar` (not by double-clicking).
  * Window opens with **Thomas the Tank Engine** in the title bar; avatar and background images show; text is readable.
  * Add one of each: `todo Buy milk`, `deadline Submit report /by 2026-09-20 1800`, `event Team sync /from 2026-09-21 1000 /to 2026-09-21 1100`, then `list` — dates should read like `Sep 20 2026, 6:00 PM`.
  * `mark 2`, `unmark 2`, `delete 1`, `undo` behave as described in the User Guide.
  * `blah` and `mark 99` give a red error bubble, not a crash.
  * `bye` closes the window; `data/tasklist.txt` appears in the folder you ran from; relaunch and `list` shows the tasks again.


Guide for testers:
* Post screenshots from your smoke tests
* Mention which OS you used for testing


</panel>

