You can use checkstyle with Gradle as a static analysis tools:

Prerequisites: 
1. Download the config files, that contains checkstyle matching CS2103T convention, from here:
https://github.com/se-edu/addressbook-level3/tree/master/config/checkstyle
2. Download the Checkstyle Plugin and configure the plugin using the steps here:
https://se-education.org/guides/tutorials/checkstyle.html

I find it especially useful to ensure that my code follows the CS2103T checkstyle convention. Putting it out here in case you miss it from the Gradle tutorial.
