Tested on **macOS 26.5.2, Apple Silicon (arm64), Azul OpenJDK 25.0.3**.

**GUI checks passed on Java 25, but a Java prerequisite mismatch was found.** Launched with `java -jar carlo.jar` in a fresh folder without existing data.

Form inputs and controls tested:
'''text
Todo: read book (Enter)
Deadline: submit report | 2026-09-25
Event: project meeting | 2026-09-22 | 2026-09-23
Invalid event: bad event | next week | 2026-09-23
Find: report
Show date: 2026-09-22
Show all
Select todo → Mark done → Unmark → Mark done
Select event → Delete
'''

- Adding a todo with Enter and deadlines/events with the form buttons worked. Find, Show date and Show all returned the expected tasks.
- Mark done, Unmark and Delete worked after selecting a task.
- The invalid event date `next week` was rejected with a date-format explanation.
- Resizing from 900 × 678 to 1100 × 600 made the tested event text fully visible; at the initial width, it extended beyond its column.
- Closing and reopening restored the marked todo and deadline; the deleted event stayed deleted.

**Issue: the documented Java minimum does not match the JAR.**

1. Use OpenJDK 21.0.9, which meets the User Guide's “Java 17 or above” requirement.
2. Run `java -jar carlo.jar`.

Expected: Carlo launches.
Actual: startup fails; the JAR uses Java 25 class files. Relevant output from `terminal-output.log`:

'''text
java.lang.UnsupportedClassVersionError: carlo/ui/Launcher has been compiled by a more recent version of the Java Runtime (class file version 69.0), this version of the Java Runtime only recognizes class file versions up to 65.0
'''

The same JAR launched successfully with Java 25.

Not verified: Full scrollbar travel was not verified. Carlo is form-based, with no command box, Send or documented `bye` command; the window close button was used.

The successful Java 25 run printed a native-access warning, but no GUI crash was encountered.


