Tested on **macOS 26.5.2, Apple Silicon (arm64), Azul OpenJDK 25.0.3**.

**GUI checks passed on Java 25, but a Java prerequisite mismatch was found.** Launched with `java -jar chim.jar` in a fresh folder without existing data.

Commands tested:
'''bash
todo read book
deadline return book /by 2019-10-15
event project meeting /from 2pm /to 4pm
priority 1 high
mark 1
list
find book
unmark 1
delete 2
mark 99
deadline test /by 2019-02-30
nonsense
todo
bye
'''

- Adding, listing, searching, marking, unmarking and deletion worked. Enter and Send both worked. Setting high priority also worked.
- Invalid inputs displayed errors without crashing.
- Resizing to 650 × 450 kept the chat readable and input accessible.
- `bye` closed Chim.
- Reopening restored the unmarked high-priority todo and event; the deleted deadline stayed deleted.

**Issue: the User Guide's Java prerequisite does not match the JAR.**

1. Use OpenJDK 21.0.9, which meets the guide's “Java 17 or above” requirement.
2. Run `java -jar chim.jar`.

Expected: Chim launches under the documented requirement.
Actual: startup fails. Relevant output from `terminal-java21.log`:

'''text
java.lang.UnsupportedClassVersionError: chim/gui/Launcher has been compiled by a more recent version of the Java Runtime (class file version 69.0), this version of the Java Runtime only recognizes class file versions up to 65.0
'''

The JAR launched successfully with Java 25, which the forum issue correctly specifies.

Not verified: The fleeting farewell text and full manual scrolling could not be verified.

The successful Java 25 run printed a native-access warning, but no GUI crash was encountered.


