Tested on **macOS 26.5.2, Apple Silicon (arm64), Azul OpenJDK 25.0.3**.

**Core smoke checks passed, but validation, exit and resource issues were found.** Launched with `java -jar florkofcows.jar` in a fresh folder without existing data.

Commands tested:
'''bash
todo read book
deadline submit report /by 2026-09-25
event camp /from 2026-09-25 0900 /to 2026-09-27 1000
list
mark 1
unmark 1
mark 2
find book
on 2026-09-26
tag 1 #fun
delete 3
todo
mark abc
event backwards /from 2026-09-27 /to 2026-09-25
deadline bad /by 2026-02-30
nonsense
list
bye
list
'''

- The welcome message and command list were readable. Adding, listing, searching, date filtering, tagging, marking, unmarking and deletion worked. Enter and Send both worked.
- Missing descriptions, non-numeric task numbers, reversed event dates and unknown commands displayed errors without crashing.
- Resizing to 700 × 500 kept the input, Send button and tested replies usable.
- After manually closing and reopening, the todo with `#fun`, completed deadline and incorrectly accepted February deadline were restored. The deleted event stayed deleted.

Issues found:

1. **Impossible date silently changed.** Enter `deadline bad /by 2026-02-30`. Expected: reject the impossible date without adding a task. Actual: `bad (by: Feb 28 2026)` is added and survives restart. See `15-command.png`.
2. **`bye` does not close the application.** Enter `bye` and wait at least 10 seconds. Expected: farewell followed by closure. Actual: `See ya!` appears, but the window remains open and had to be closed manually. See `94-bye-still-open.png`.
3. **Missing stylesheet reported on launch.** Run `java -jar florkofcows.jar` in a fresh folder. Expected: bundled stylesheets load without missing-resource messages. Actual: the GUI launches, but the log prints `Could not find stylesheet: jar:file:/Users/claudedev/Desktop/FlorkOfCows-smoke-test/florkofcows.jar!/main.css`. No specific visual defect is attributed to this warning.

The log also repeatedly prints `Loading FXML document with JavaFX API of version 26 by JavaFX runtime of version 25.0.3`. The app remained usable on this runtime.

Not verified: scrolling; the mouse-wheel attempt did not produce visible movement, so it is not classified as an application bug.

The terminal also printed a JavaFX native-access warning, but it did not prevent launch. No crashes encountered.

