* Link to User Guide: https://minhhoanglenus.github.io/ip/
* Which OS'es to test on: Mac | Linux
* Things to check specifically:
  * Use Java 25.
  * Download `Aster.jar` and put it in a new empty folder.
  * Confirm the downloaded file has SHA-256:
    `f12c28b195a00865b311996a89a6a1c3572b42154da4a4b9f907f5a989b3abb8`
  * Run `java -jar Aster.jar`.
  * Confirm that the Aster GUI opens.
  * Run `todo test task`.
  * Run `deadline submit report /by 2026-09-20`.
  * Run `list` and confirm that both tasks appear.
  * Close Aster, launch the same JAR again, and confirm that the tasks reload.
  * Run `bye` and confirm that Aster closes by itself.

Guide for testers:

* Post screenshots from your smoke tests.
* Mention which OS and CPU architecture you used.
* Include the output of `java -version`.
* Confirm whether the SHA-256 matched.
* Report whether every check passed, or provide the complete error output if anything failed.
