<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/93" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**2. :fas-info-circle: Clarification on Week 3 iP catch-up deadline**
</div>

The Weekly Schedule states that work completed after Friday 1600 will be credited to the following week. The course policy also states that weekly project deliverables without specific deadlines are flexible and that students will not be penalized if they catch up within a few days.

The Week 3 iP instructions do not appear to specify a separate hard deadline. Could you please confirm whether completing and pushing all Week 3 iP requirements by Sunday, 30 August, will be treated as catching up within a few days without penalty, although the work may be credited to the following week?

Thank you.
</panel>

<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/368#issuecomment-5720768849" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**3 :fas-comment:**
</div>

Hi @aanya007, I tested murphy.jar on Windows 11 x64 with Oracle JDK 25.0.4, running java -jar murphy.jar from a new empty folder. It exits immediately with NoClassDefFoundError: javafx/application/Application, so I couldn't reach the GUI or test the commands and persistence.

I checked the JAR contents and found that javafx.graphics and javafx.fxml are missing, which is also consistent with the Linux launch failure reported above. You may want to check that build.gradle includes the JavaFX graphics and FXML dependencies for Windows, macOS and Linux, then rebuild the fat JAR.

Screenshots attached.

