Tested Bean Bot v0.2.0 on Windows 11 with Oracle JDK 25.0.4.

* Creation, all documented aliases, priority sorting/colours, mark/unmark, deletion and persistence worked correctly. `exit`, `q`, and closing with the X button all saved the tasks, and the `secret` argument worked (`COOL BEANS`).
* On my 1366×768 display, the default 600×800 window opened partly off-screen: the title bar was above the screen and the input area was behind the taskbar, so I could not resize or move it normally with the mouse.
* An event ending before it starts was accepted: `event backwards /from 2026-10-10 /to 2026-10-01`. The other invalid dates, names, priorities and indices were rejected clearly.
* `find` works for case-insensitive keywords, substrings and phrases, but not misspellings such as `reprot`; this may be intended because the User Guide only promises keyword search. However, a search with no matches says “No tasks yet” even when tasks exist, and search results are renumbered from 1 independently of the main list, which can be misleading when using `mark` or `delete`.

Screenshots attached. I otherwise found the interface clear and the priority colours useful.

