Smoke tested Moon on Windows 11 with Java 25.0.4 — the night-sky UI is lovely. The jar launched straight away, and to-dos, deadlines and events all added fine (I first tried an event with times and got a clear yyyy-MM-dd reminder, which matches your UG since events take dates only). list, find, mark, unmark, delete and undo all did what they should, the chat scrolled to the newest reply each time, and my three tasks with the done tick came back after a restart. `bye` closed it immediately in both runs.

Error handling is solid too: `blah`, `2026-02-30`, `mark 99`, a bare `todo` and an event with `/from` after `/to` each got their own "Oof!" message and left the list untouched. One behaviour worth knowing: if a command fails (my `delete 3` when only 2 tasks existed), a following `undo` rewinds the last *successful* command instead, so it undid my earlier `mark`. Screenshots attached!

