Tested on Windows 11 with Java 25.0.4, using the newer LinuxBugFix jar rather than the A-FinalRelease link. It launched fine, all four task types worked (the `[C]` constraints with their triggers are a neat idea), and list/mark/unmark/delete/find behaved. All three `/afterdate` formats were accepted — `16/5`, `16/5/27` and `16/05/2027 0830` — and anything without a time defaulted to 11:59PM as documented. Both moods showed up: across about 20 replies I got roughly 6 gold "Your Majesty" ones and the rest red "bestie/no cap" ones. Tasks survived a restart, and invalid input (including an event ending before it starts) never crashed it.

