**1. :fas-info-circle: Request to help with smoke testing JAR file**
</div>

## Smoke testing help pleasee 😄 

Please help smoke test the Zikiai v0.3.0 JAR on Windows, macOS, or Linux.

### Preparation

1. Install Java 25.
2. Download `zikiai.jar` from the v0.3.0 release 
3. Place it in an empty folder.
4. Open a terminal in that folder and run:

'''bash
java -jar "zikiai.jar"
'''

## Links 

1. Link to user guide:  https://zikiai.github.io/ip/
2. Link to v0.3.0 release: https://github.com/zikiai/ip/releases/tag/v0.3.0

I am not sure but maybe can ask AI to help with the smoke test, I need to confirm that .jar file works on other environments. 

### Test checklist

Please check that:

- [ ] The GUI opens without an error.
- [ ] The complete Zikiai window is displayed correctly.
- [ ] `todo read book` adds a task.
- [ ] `deadline submit report /by 2026-09-30` adds a deadline.
- [ ] `event meeting /from 2pm /to 4pm` adds an event.
- [ ] `list` displays the tasks.
- [ ] `priority 1 high` updates the task’s priority.
- [ ] `mark 1` marks the task as completed.
- [ ] `find book` finds the matching task.
- [ ] An invalid command displays a helpful error without closing the app.
- [ ] Closing and reopening Zikiai preserves the saved tasks.
- [ ] `bye` ends the session and disables further input. (it is not designed to close yet, but I will add that)

### Results

Feel free to use this format:

'''text
Operating system:
JAR launched successfully: Yes/No
Checklist items that failed:
Error message, if any:
Additional observations:
'''

If anything fails, please attach a screenshot and include the complete error message shown in the terminal.
</panel>

