For the description after the parameter name, I don’t think capitalization is explicitly required. The SE-EDU coding standard requires each parameter description to end with punctuation, but it does not state that the description must begin with a capital letter.

For example, this should be acceptable:

'''java
@param task task to add.
'''

The example in the guide uses capitalization, so using `Task to add.` may be preferable for consistency, but I would treat that as a style choice rather than a strict rule. In my project, I used lowercase descriptions.
</panel>

