<div slot="header">

**48 :fas-comment:**
</div>

I think a small PR for the shared interface change makes sense if both features genuinely need the same change. Merging that first would give both branches a common base and reduce the chance of conflicts in `Model.java` / `ModelManager.java`.

I don’t think every PR necessarily needs to introduce user-visible functionality, as long as the change is self-contained, tested, and doesn’t leave the codebase in a broken or awkward intermediate state. In this case, if the interface change can stand on its own cleanly, separating it seems preferable to having both feature PRs independently modify the same shared files.

If the interface change only makes sense together with one particular feature, though, then I’d probably keep it within that feature PR instead of creating plumbing purely for hypothetical future use.
</panel>

