**1. :fas-info-circle: Warnings when running iP JAR files**
</div>

Hello, I think this is a warning that has been popping up for quite a few user's code, including mine.

When I run my code (or smoke test other's code), I have these warnings.

```
WARNING: A restricted method in java.lang.System has been called
WARNING: java.lang.System::load has been called by com.sun.glass.utils.NativeLibLoader in module javafx.graphics (jrt:/javafx.graphics)
WARNING: Use --enable-native-access=javafx.graphics to avoid a warning for callers in this module
WARNING: Restricted methods will be blocked in a future release unless native access is enabled
```

To my knowledge, it is because newer Java versions (22+) have stricter boundaries regarding loading native libraries, which JavaFX uses.

Are these warnings alright, or should we do something to fix them?
I know its a console warning and the app still functions.

And you can simply add a flag to disable before the -jar argument:

```
java --enable-native-access=javafx.graphics -jar YOUR_JAR_NAME.jar
```
</panel>

