@Brendan-Lim As Prof @damithc , @dillionlim and @spencercdz have mentioned, I also personally think it is good to remove those side classes/ methods/ attributes because the essence of the UML diagram is to show the main overview details of how it functions.

You can have multiple UML diagrams to show specific linkages per say. And in either case, you can add a note for readers on whats not present. Or just title the UML diagram properly like "UML Class Diagram of XXX Method" so that each UML diagram shows a specific single, identifiable purpose.

