You're right that extracting each branch into separate methods improves SLAP. It hides the lower level execution logic and makes a lot of sense in making the `getResponse()` method easier to read. But I feel that every time u add a new command, there's a chance you accidentally introduce a bug in your if-else logic. 

Thinking about an abstract Command is a good way to prevent that. You may want to read #69 (Command Logic) & #75 (Parser Logic). This makes sure the Parser is in-charge of returning a new Command object, and your Command object can contain states (i.e., index to mark, etc)
</panel>

