Just to be clear, the word right after the **@PARAM** tag is the name of the parameter itself.

I'm assuming that you are talking about the word after that instead, in which case I could not find a hard rule about whether it should be capitalised or not in the [coding standard guide](https://se-education.org/guides/conventions/java/intermediate.html). The only rule I could find was that there needs to be a [punctuation at the end of each parameter description](https://se-education.org/guides/conventions/java/intermediate.html#:~:text=Punctuation%20behind%20each%20parameter%20description.). 

However, the [worked example](https://se-education.org/guides/conventions/java/intermediate.html#:~:text=%40param%20x%20X,zone%20is%20%3C%3D%200.) in the guide does indeed show that the first word of the description is capitalised, presumably to follow proper sentence structure and grammar. To be safe, I would follow the worked example and capitalise the first letter of the word that follows after the parameter name.

I would like to hear what other people have done regarding this as well in their own iP!


</panel>

