Hi I think when we are checking for which functions are callbacks, we only need to concern ourselves with the call direction and nesting of the function within the diagram. So whether `Parser` got its handle on `ParserFactory` through an explicit constructor parameter, a stored back-reference or any other way, it doesn't change the fact that the callee(`Parser`) is invoking a method on its own caller(`ParserFactory`) mid-call.

Hope this helps and I am interested in knowing what others think as well!
