* Things to check specifically:

- The released JAR launches successfully and opens the GUI.
- Adding to-do, deadline, and event tasks (using yyyy-MM-dd HHmm format).
- Listing all tasks (list) and finding tasks by keyword (find).
- Marking (mark) and unmarking (unmark) tasks as complete.
- Deleting tasks (delete).
- Adding, listing, finding, and deleting clients (client, clients, findclient, deleteclient).
- Saving data automatically and loading tasks/clients correctly after restarting Wiz.
- Invalid commands, date formats, out-of-range indices, and missing inputs show helpful error messages without crashing.
- The GUI displays messages/avatars correctly and auto-scrolls to the newest message.
- The bye command exits the application cleanly.



Guide for testers:
* Post screenshots from your smoke tests
* Mention which OS you used for testing


