Key point should be that `getInfo()` can still act as a callback even if the method itself is not passed directly. If `ParserFactory` passes a reference to itself, like `new Parser(this)`, then `Parser` can later call `getInfo()` through that reference.

So I agree that showing how `Parser` gets access to `ParserFactory` would make the diagram clearer, but I don’t think it necessarily has to be written as `Parser(getInfo)`.

</panel>

