<div slot="header">

**23 :fas-comment:**
</div>

“all hardware is in working order” feels too broad to be useful as a precondition since it would apply to almost every use case anyway.

A better precondition IMO should describe some specific state that must already be true before that particular use case starts, such as the machine being idle with no transaction in progress. If theres no meaningful condition that is unique to the use case thrn it probably makes more sense to leave the precondition out rather than adding a generic system assumption.

</panel>

<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/540#issuecomment-5789735536" expanded>
