Thank you for the clarification @spencercdz @dillionlim. On the topic about diagram consistency, I have a follow-up question.

If we intentionally include more details for certain classes that are the main focus of the diagram, while treating other classes as black boxes, how will the reader know that missing methods or attributes were omitted on purpose, rather than negligence? Or should we remain consistent and include all details for all classes, even if private methods for black boxed classes do not add value to our understanding in the diagram?

Like if `Parser` show some important private methods and constructors, but `Storage` class only shows the class name because the private methods, constructors and fields are irrelevant, how do we show the private methods in `Storage` were purposefully left out?

