One failure mode I've run into with coding agents is treating **"the tool couldn't observe it"** as **"the app is broken"**. This can happen during GUI testing when the agent does not have the same screen or accessibility access as a normal user.

Before reporting a bug, I now ask it to separate:

1. what it directly observed,
2. what it is only inferring, and
3. one independent way to reproduce the result outside the agent's test environment.

A quick follow-up prompt is: `List the observations, hypotheses, and an independent reproduction step separately.`

This helped me avoid posting a potentially misleading JavaFX bug report today. The limitation was in the testing setup, so the app itself had not been proven faulty.

