<div slot="header">

**20 :fas-comment:**
</div>

One distinction that may help is that the Features section in the User Guide is also a way of organising user-facing documentation, so I wouldn't assume that every subsection there necessarily maps 1-to-1 to a feature we should claim in the TP feature list.

For the TP, I think it is safer to describe a feature in terms of an observable capability/behaviour the product commits to providing. Instructions such as manually editing the data file can still be documented, but whether they count as a product feature depends on whether the application deliberately supports and guarantees that workflow.
</panel>

