<div slot="header">

**4. :fas-info-circle: Request to help with smoke testing JAR file**
</div>

* Link to JAR file: https://github.com/adwaithanoop/ip/releases/tag/v0.1
* Link to the User Guide: https://adwaithanoop.github.io/ip/
* Which OS'es to test on: Windows | Mac | Linux
* Things to check specifically: Try to crash the program, or any ways of adding / editing tasks that result in the task not being saved.


Guide for testers:
* Post screenshots from your smoke tests of each round
* Mention which OS you used for testing

Try these:

Round 1 adding and listing
```
todo borrow book
deadline return book /by 2026-12-02 1800
event project meeting /from 2026-12-02 1400 /to 2026-12-02 1600
event orientation week /from 2026-10-05 /to 2026-10-09
mark 1
list
```
Round 2 editing and searching

```
edit 2 /by 2026-12-05
on 2026-12-02
next 2
find book
```
Round 3 error handling

```
todo
mark 99
deadline submit report /by tomorrow
blah
```
Lastly,
```
bye
```

Then start Bob again in the same folder and type `list` — all four tasks should still be there, with `borrow book` still marked done.

</panel>

