<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/145#issuecomment-5537514081" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**12 :fas-comment:**
</div>

To add on to @less413 's point, I believe there was a way to uncommit commits that was taught in the gitmastery.

But here's hopefully a way that can help solve your issue?
git branch branch-Level-10 (To create the branch)
git reset --hard HEAD~1 (To uncommit and revert back to unstaged version) [i'm assuming it's just one commit so far?]
git push origin master --force-with-lease (Since master was already pushed, you now need to force-push to make the remote match)
git checkout branch-Level-10
git push -u origin branch-Level-10


To check if it works as expected, you can run these:
git log --oneline main          # commit should be gone
git log --oneline branch-Level-10   # commit should be there
git status                       # working directory should be clean

Hope this works!

</panel>

