<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/216#issuecomment-5676285764" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**17 :fas-comment:**
</div>

My take is if something value adds the product then it counts as a feature, it doesn't matter whether its triggered by a command, automatic, or doesn't even happen on the app. So both saving and editing the data file would count as features for me.

Saving obviously value adds because your data persists without you needing to think about it. Editing the data file directly is less obvious since the app has no code for it, but I'd say it still value adds because it lets fast typists or power users manage their data without going through the app UI at all. That benefit only exists because of a deliberate choice to use a plaintext format.

So for me the trigger mechanism doesn't really matter, the test is just whether it makes the product better for the user to use
</panel>

