<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/547" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**1. :fas-info-circle: What makes a partial tP PR meaningful if it doesnt complete a feature end-to-end?**
</div>

the [integration notes](https://nus-cs2103-ay2627-s1.github.io/website/schedule/week7/topics.html#w7-6-integration-approaches) recommend early, frequent, and incremental integration. the [v1.2 instructions](https://nus-cs2103-ay2627-s1.github.io/website/schedule/week8/project.html#3-add-the-first-functionality-increment-thu-oct-8th-23-59) also say that a PR can contain a small code change rather than a complete end-to-end feature, as long as it moves the codebase forward meaningfully without breaking it.

say a feature needs a new model class, parser and command changes, and UI support. one possible first PR adds only the model class and its tests, even though no existing user flow uses it yet. another option is a thin usable path through all those layers, but that PR could be larger.

what criteria should we use to decide whether a PR is meaningful enough to merge? 
</panel>

<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/258" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**2. :fas-info-circle: Request to help with smoke testing JAR file**
</div>

- Link to JAR file: https://github.com/suvan1911/ip/releases/latest/download/LenZaBot.jar
- Link to the User Guide: https://suvan1911.github.io/ip/
- Java version required: Java 25
- Which OS'es to test on: Windows | Mac | Linux
- Already tested on: Windows

Things to check specifically:
1. Place `LenZaBot.jar` in a new empty folder.
2. Open a terminal in that folder and run `java -jar LenZaBot.jar`.
3. Confirm that the GUI opens and displays the LenZaBot title.
4. Try `todo`, `deadline`, `event`, `list`, `mark`, `unmark`, `delete`, and `find` as described in the User Guide.
5. Try an invalid command and an event whose end is before its start. Confirm that a highlighted error appears and the application does not crash.
6. Resize the window and confirm that messages remain readable.
7. Close and reopen LenZaBot, then use `list` to confirm that tasks were saved.
8. Enter `bye` and confirm that the farewell appears before the window closes.

Guide for testers:
- Post screenshots from your smoke test.
- Mention the operating system and Java version used.
- Report any command or feature that did not work.
- Include reproduction steps and expected versus actual behavior for any problem.

Thank you!

</panel>

<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/145" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**3. :fas-info-circle: Forgot to do Level 10 of iP in a separate branch**
</div>

Hi, 

I forgot to create a separate branch named `branch-Level-10` for Level 10 and accidentally committed directly to master. 

What should I do now?
</panel>

<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/145#issuecomment-5537707128" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**4 :fas-comment:**
</div>

Thank you all for your help! I fixed the issue by preserving the Level 10 work on a branch, resetting master to the previous commit, merging the branch back with `--no-ff`, and moving the `Level-10` tag to the new merge commit. :D
</panel>

<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/146#issuecomment-5537781260" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**5 :fas-comment:**
</div>

Alternatively, you could also try making a git alias that runs a shell function. This gives you more freedom to make more custom scripts to suit your needs in the future.

`git config --global alias.acp '!f() ``{`` git add . && git commit -m "$1" && git push; ``}``; f'`

Then you can do 
`git acp "my commit message"`

which would be equivalent to 

```
git add .
git commit -m "my commit message"
git push
```
</panel>

<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/162#issuecomment-5568898725" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**6 :fas-comment:**
</div>

from what i understand, using a PR is optional, but if you do use one, the extension should eventually be merged into `master`. An open PR only proposes the change, so the extension still isn't part of the main version of the iP.

The [Week 5 instructions](https://nus-cs2103-ay2627-s1.github.io/website/admin/ip-w5.html#5-add-an-extension) say that a branch is recommended and that we “may add it via a PR”. They also require the relevant commit to be tagged `BCD-Extension`, so i'd merge the PR after reviewing it, then tag the corresponding commit and push the tag.
</panel>

