<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/201" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**3. :fas-info-circle: What counts as a feature in the MVP?**
</div>

In [Task 2](https://nus-cs2103-ay2627-s1.github.io/website/schedule/week6/project.html#2-draft-the-feature-specification-sun-sep-20th-23-59) section of this week's TP tasks, it states that 

> For each feature, specify all of the following:
> 
> Feature: Name of the feature e.g., Add contact
> Purpose: What it does
>
> Command format: The precise format of the command.
> Example commands: (to show how the command is used)
> ...

This seems to imply that features in the MVP must be associated with commands. Does this mean more general points for what the MVP should have such as "command-based navigation" (only using keyboard commands to navigate the app) or "data persistence" (storing the data somewhere so it is saved and can be loaded when you start the app again next session) should not be listed as features?
</panel>

