<div slot="header">

**5. :fas-info-circle: JavaFX Tutorial - Unable to limit Window size**
</div>

### Issue

I am following JavaFX Tutorial Part 5’s “Setting limit to Window size” section. Below is my code for the `start` method:

'''java
@Override
public void start(Stage stage) ``{``
    try ``{``
        FXMLLoader fxmlLoader = new FXMLLoader(Main.class.getResource("/view/MainWindow.fxml"));
        AnchorPane ap = fxmlLoader.load();
        Scene scene = new Scene(ap);
        stage.setScene(scene);
        stage.setTitle("Duke");
        stage.getIcons().add(new Image(Main.class.getResourceAsStream("/images/DaDuke.png")));
        stage.setMinHeight(220);
        stage.setMinWidth(417);
        fxmlLoader.<MainWindow>getController().setDuke(duke);  // inject the Duke instance
        stage.show();
    ``}`` catch (IOException e) ``{``
        e.printStackTrace();
    ``}``
``}``
'''

However, after launching the GUI, I can still resize the window below those dimensions. I expected the window to stop shrinking at the specified minimum width and height. Attached is an image showing the window shrinking to a size that is definitely less than 417 x 220.

<img width="588" height="362" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/93ba43f8-c823-4f6c-b65e-2769acab7311" />

Is there any additional setup required for these limits to take effect, or could this be related to my environment?

### Environment
- OS: Ubuntu 24.04.4 LTS running under WSL2
- Java: OpenJDK 25.0.3
- JavaFX: 17.0.7
- Gradle wrapper: 9.6.1
- Terminal: Bash

### Recreation
1. Follow the JavaFX Tutorial Part 5 window-size instructions.
2. Add `stage.setMinHeight(220)` and `stage.setMinWidth(417)` before `stage.show()`.
3. Launch the GUI and resize it to be smaller than the configured limits.
4. Observe that the window resize is not prevented.

Thanks!
</panel>

