> I'm curious about the last parenthesised part, what long non-method thing would need to exist?

What I have in mind is a map "registry" that maps a "string" (the split string) to the function (a callable perhaps). You realize it's either the case where you exhaust the patterns in the switch expression, or you use a hash map that does the mapping. The parenthesised part refers to the latter.

