<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/166#issuecomment-5586101808" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**4 :fas-comment:**
</div>

Worth noting is that if attempts on refactors changes the structure too much, even if the code becomes easier to read/is more efficient, there might be a code regression where edge cases which works on your original code no longer works on the new code. So code refactoring should usually be done with java tests, without them it is probably better to leave them as they are.
</panel>

