<div slot="header">

**8 :fas-comment:**
</div>

I think even with separate Command classes, the parser still needs to decide which command to create, so the if-else/switch might just move there. The benefit is that you can understand and change each command’s behaviour separately. 
E.g. changing how `delete` works wouldn’t require going through the code for `find` or `mark`. So I’d judge the refactoring by whether it makes those changes easier, rather than whether it gets rid of the if-else chain.
</panel>

