I think `getInfo()` can be both a public method and a callback here, since being public is about who can access it, while callback would describe how it’s used in this interaction.

Saw in similar example in the week 6 notes under self-invocation: 
`Book.write()` calls `Chapter.getText()`, which then calls `getAuthor()` on the original Book object. 
I think the same idea applies here, since `Parser` calls back to `ParserFactory`, even without explicitly showing a function being passed as a parameter.
</panel>

