<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/328" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**4. :fas-info-circle: Smoke-testing request: Glennon on Windows/Linux (Java 25)**
</div>

Hi everyone! Could someone help smoke-test **Glennon**, my task manager, on **Windows or Linux (x64) with Java 25**? It has passed local testing on macOS using Zulu FX JDK 25.0.3.

* Link to JAR file: [Glennon-smoke-test.jar](https://github.com/ultramanarm/ip/releases/download/A-Jar/Glennon-smoke-test.jar)
* Link to the User Guide: [Glennon User Guide](https://github.com/ultramanarm/ip/blob/master/docs/README.md)
* Which OS'es to test on: **Windows / Linux (x64)**
* Things to check specifically:
  1. Put the JAR in an empty folder. Open a terminal there and run `java -version` to confirm Java 25, then `java -jar "Glennon-smoke-test.jar"`.
  2. Check that the window, images, and input controls load correctly. Try adding, listing, marking, and deleting missions using the user guide.
  3. Try an invalid command such as `delete 99` and check that the app reports an error and remains usable.
  4. Enter `bye`, reopen the JAR from the same folder, and check that remaining missions and completion status are restored.
  5. Resize the window and check that long messages remain readable.

Guide for testers:
* Please post screenshots from your smoke tests.
* Mention your OS, CPU architecture, and `java -version` output.
* If anything fails, please include the command you entered and any terminal error output.

Please use the JAR launch command above for this test; the user guide's Quick Start describes launching from source on macOS.

Thanks for your help!

</panel>

<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/27#issuecomment-5333061864" expanded>
