One thing I noticed with `tasks`: with an undated todo, a deadline on 16 Oct and an event on 15 Oct, `tasks 2026-10-17` still showed the undated todo under “tasks happening on Oct 17”. `tasks 2026-10-15` also included that todo alongside the event, whereas the [user guide example](https://denzelgoo.github.io/ip/) shows only the event. If todos are meant to appear on every date, it would help to clarify this in the guide.

I also saw the JavaFX native-access warning at startup and chat replies printed in the terminal, but no crash during these checks.

Testing note: the interactive checks used the unchanged release JAR in a temporary macOS launcher with the same Zulu FX runtime. The complete plain-`java -jar` GUI workflow was not independently verified.


