<div slot="header">

**4 :fas-comment:**
</div>

I think it can be worded such that after a squash merge, you typically delete the source branch to keep the repository clean. The destination branch maintains a clean, linear history because all changes from the source branch were consolidated into a single commit, rather than retaining every individual commit.

Would that be clearer?
</panel>

