<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/219#issuecomment-5678048973" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**13 :fas-comment:**
</div>

My view is that we should sorta follow the "happy path" principle in W5.4, where we make the path where everything goes well the first alt condition. Then, we only include highly relevant different paths where the response of our architecture makes a big difference (e.g. if alt 2, then execute method X). 

Thus we convey the main essence of our architecture, omitting irrelevant edge cases and "exhausting" all cases like what the others had mentioned.  
</panel>

