<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/143" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**2. :fas-info-circle: [Suggestion] Update Gradle Checkstyle version**
</div>

When attempting the `A-CheckStyle` increment, I (Codex) ran into this issue:

```
• The integration itself is active, and it exposed two issues: [omitted], while
  the main-source scan hit an execution error rather than a normal style
  failure. I’m diagnosing the latter before deciding whether any source
  formatting changes are needed.
```

```
• The main-source failure is a known limitation of Checkstyle 11.0.0: it cannot
  parse Java 25’s flexible constructor bodies, which this project uses. I’m
  updating only the tool version—not the SE-EDU ruleset—to a Java-25-capable
  release, then I’ll reassess the actual style findings.
```

With Codex ending up choosing version 14.1.0:

```
- Used Checkstyle 14.1.0 because 11.0.0 cannot parse this project’s Java 25
  flexible constructor bodies. Checkstyle added support in 13.5.0
  (https://checkstyle.org/release-notes.html).
```

I'm wondering if the Checkstyle version provided in the [guide](https://se-education.org/guides/tutorials/checkstyle.html) could be updated to account for Java 25, or whether that would unintentionally break any part of `checkstyle.xml`, since it is also mentioned in the guide that

> Reason: checkstyle.xml is written for a particular version, but the plugin was not configured to the correct version.

Preliminarily, no issues have been discovered by me or Codex.

Thank you!
</panel>

<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/25" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**3. :fas-info-circle: W1.2d minor correction**
</div>

In Week 1 notes, under the section on [subclass constructors](https://nus-cs2103-ay2627-s1.github.io/website/schedule/week1/topics.html#subclass-constructors):

> Invocation of a superclass constructor must be the first line in the subclass constructor.

This is no longer true in Java 25, per [Oracle docs](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/25/language/flexible-constructor-bodies.html).

Minor nitpick, but is potentially relevant since this course uses Java 25 by default.
</panel>

<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/25#issuecomment-5326046942" expanded>
