Thanks for all the feedback. What I did in the end was something like that but more tedious.

I made a Functional Interface called GuiListener.  This comes from my Chatbot class (Main entry point).
```
    public void start(Stage stage) ``{``
        gui = new Gui();
        gui.attachInputListener((GuiListener) this::inputListener);

        Scene scene = new Scene(gui);
        stage.show();
    ``}``
```
Instead of button handling inputs, onclick it tells the listeners that "hey there is input from user" by feeding it to the listener.
The listener will then do whatever it needs to. 

I think here the difference is that I have an extra layer that bridges Logic and GUI that originates from Chatbot.java. instead of being part of GUI or Logic.
</panel>

