<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/341" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**1. :fas-info-circle: Request to help with smoke testing JAR file**
</div>

Link to JAR file: https://github.com/DhruvBawa/ip/releases/latest
Link to the User Guide: https://dhruvbawa.github.io/ip/
Which OS'es to test on: Windows | Mac


* Things to check specifically:
  * The JAR launches successfully using Java 25.
  * The interface, custom font, background, and messages display correctly.
  * Try adding, listing, editing, finding, marking, unmarking, and deleting tasks.
  * Try deadlines and events using the date/time formats in the User Guide.
  * Restart the app and confirm saved tasks are restored.
  * Try a few invalid commands and check that the app shows a helpful error without crashing.
  * Check that both pressing Enter and clicking Send submit a command.

Guide for testers:

* Post screenshots from your smoke tests.
* Mention which OS and Java version you used.
* Report the exact command entered if anything behaves unexpectedly.

</panel>

<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/229#issuecomment-5692804859" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**2 :fas-comment:**
</div>

Tested on Arch Linux, OpenJDK 25.0.2.
I encountered the following issues during testing:

### 1. Tasks containing | are corrupted or lost after restarting

I added tasks with descriptions such as tea | coffee (todo), fish | chips (event), and elon | musk (deadline). All appeared correctly before restarting.

After closing and relaunching the JAR:
- Todo descriptions were truncated to the text before |. For example, tea | coffee became tea.
- The event and deadline tasks containing | disappeared entirely.

<img width="1422" height="1724" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8b236d7e-d0f1-469a-a483-e2657d0eb421" />

<img width="1422" height="1724" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7b1fa748-23eb-467f-bd2e-2cf190c08d95" />

### 2. Extra whitespace in replies
Some replies contain unusually large gaps between words, as shown in the image below

### 3. The bye command does not close the application
Entering bye displays a farewell message, but the GUI remains open. I can still add and edit tasks afterwards

<img width="2880" height="1800" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/29648fd2-0f46-417b-b526-40c4f2cf5bb9" />

</panel>

<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/258#issuecomment-5693049172" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**3 :fas-comment:**
</div>

Tested on Arch Linux, OpenJDK 25.0.2.

The GUI launched successfully. Basic task commands, highlighted errors for invalid commands and reversed event dates, window resizing, and saving ordinary tasks worked during testing. The `bye` command displayed a farewell before closing the window.

I found a saving issue with deadline and event descriptions ending in a space followed by `|`.

### Steps to reproduce:

1. Enter these commands:

   '''text
   deadline trailing | /by 2026-09-30
   event trailing | /from 2026-09-20 /to 2026-09-21
   list
   '''

2. Both tasks are accepted and displayed in the list.
3. Close and reopen LenZaBot from the same folder, then enter `list`.

**Expected:** Both accepted tasks remain available after restarting. If these descriptions are unsupported, the app should reject them when entered.

**Actual:** Both tasks disappear. On startup, LenZaBot displays `Skipped 2 damaged line(s) in the save file.`, and `list` shows an empty task list.

Descriptions containing ` | ` in the middle are rejected correctly
this issue occurs when the description ends with ` |`.

**Before restarting:**

<img width="1422" height="856" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dc8fabe6-2900-479c-ad62-8a35bfec64de" />

**After restarting:**

<img width="1422" height="856" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6e3019af-ee05-42bb-b4a8-b2a0e516cf2a" />

</panel>

<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/286#issuecomment-5696703724" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**4 :fas-comment:**
</div>

Tested on Arch Linux with OpenJDK 25.0.2.

The app launched successfully, and I didn’t encounter any major issues. Adding, listing, finding, marking, unmarking, and deleting tasks worked as expected. I also tried the command aliases and statistics feature.

Invalid commands and dates were handled without crashing. Tasks and completion status were preserved after restarting, including descriptions containing |. The GUI remained responsive, and long messages stayed readable when I resized the window.

A few small/niche things I noticed: 
- When find returns no matches, it only shows “Here are the matching tasks in your list:”. A “No matching tasks found” message would make this clearer.
- bye closes the window immediately, so there isn’t time to read the farewell message
- text does not resize with the window it so when the window is large the text gets harder to read
- You are able to send messages by pressing enter without having any text written. Pressing and holding enter made it continually send a blank input and after a few seconds of holding down the enter button the app started to slow down and lag. Eventually it crashed
- Also noticed that text does not wrap when entering a long string of text. Making it wrap would increase readability

Otherwise, the smoke tests went smoothly.

<img width="1422" height="1724" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6952ed45-5e5c-4694-a68b-feda52da717a" />

<img width="520" height="680" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c123c5ac-45df-4cc1-a198-35f16af0556b" />
</panel>

<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/315#issuecomment-5708913625" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**5 :fas-comment:**
</div>

Tested on Arch Linux, using OpenJDK 25.0.2.

The JAR opened successfully with `java -jar nubish.jar` from a new folder. The normal task commands worked, and tasks were saved after closing and reopening the app. Invalid dates, reversed event times, duplicate descriptions, and descriptions containing `|` were rejected correctly. 

I found a few minor issues:

1. Entering `mark 2147483648`, `unmark 2147483648`, or `delete 2147483648` produces no reply in the GUI (2147483648 is 1 greater than the max integer value). I expected an invalid-task-number error. The terminal shows a `NumberFormatException`. The app still accepts commands afterwards.


<img width="848" height="922" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/10bd76c8-3e0b-465d-b95f-29a2b008bf52" />


2. `bye` displays the farewell and disables the input box, but the window stays open even after waiting several seconds. The guide describes this as exiting Nubish, so I had expected the window to close.

<img width="848" height="922" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a9ad3217-b023-4c8b-b424-91e872daf05b" />

3. ASCII art was not rendered properly unfortunately

Then i have 1 small suggestion: 

Search result numbering can be confusing. With `todo apples` followed by `todo bananas`, `find bananas` shows bananas as number 1. Entering `mark 1` then marks apples. The guide does say to use numbers from `list`, but keeping the original numbers in search results after the find would help avoid mistakes.

<img width="848" height="922" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ad1db3c4-aaf6-42ac-b1a8-cd3e4d2ec239" />
</panel>

<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/341#issuecomment-5709254457" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**6 :fas-comment:**
</div>

@wangyixuan818 @qqnoodle Thanks for the quick response. The `bye` command is meant to close after a delay. specifically after 5.0 seconds. if possible could you check that the delay you found was 5 seconds long and not any longer
</panel>

