Tested on Arch Linux, using OpenJDK 25.0.2.

The JAR launched successfully. The normal commands, sorting, reminders, resizing, and saving after closing/reopening worked. Invalid commands and dates showed red error messages, and `bye` displayed the farewell before closing.

I found a saving issue with `|` in task descriptions. To reproduce, start with an empty list and enter:

'''text
todo ordinary task
todo tea | coffee
deadline elon | musk /by 21/9/2026 1800
event fish | chips /from 20/9/2026 1400 /to 20/9/2026 1600
'''

All four tasks are accepted. After closing and reopening from the same folder, `list` is empty, including the ordinary task without a pipe. I expected the tasks to remain unchanged, or the character to be rejected when adding them.

The loading error only appears in the terminal. Adding another task afterwards also overwrites the old save, so this can lead to permanent loss of the previous tasks.


<img width="848" height="922" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/53564dd1-55ed-45cf-a6cb-e1e810586f17" />

