@damithc apologies I think my wording should've been more clear

What I meant to say is the text associated with the indicators differ based on whether the requirement is done or not

for example, for `Merging PRs`,

- if it's not done it shows "At least 1 PR(s) merged in own fork: **not done**"
- if it's done it shows "At least 1 PR(s) merged in own fork: **done**"

however, for `JavaFX Tutorial`, it will always show

> "Did all 5 parts of the JavaFX tutorial (i.e., you have a fork named javafx-tutorial and it has tags Tutorial-Part1..Tutorial-Part5)"

regardless of whether or not the increment was actually done or not

I was confused by this because I had done the JavaFX Tutorial but made a typo in one of my tag names (mispelled `Tutorial`). As such, the indicator (rightfully) showed up as red, yet the description (incorrectly) suggested that I had already tagged the commits correctly.

I feel like if the JavaFX Tutorial isn't done, the description should instead read:

> "Did all 5 parts of the JavaFX tutorial (i.e., you have a fork named javafx-tutorial and it has tags Tutorial-Part1..Tutorial-Part5)**: not done**"

for consistency with the other increments



EDIT: upon further inspection i noticed some other increments' descriptions also don't make the above distinction (e.g. the GM Tours), so i guess this issue was really more nitpicky than i originally thought, still i think they should be changed for the sake of consistency as most of the other descriptions do make that distinction
</panel>

