One practical reason to keep @Override is that it catches typos. If you accidentally wrote hashcode() instead of hashCode(), Java would otherwise treat it as a new method and still use Object.hashCode(). With @Override, you get a compiler error straight away.
</panel>

<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/297#issuecomment-5730770392" expanded>
