One small Java detail: making getInfo() public means Parser is allowed to call it, but Parser still needs a reference to the ParserFactory object (assuming getInfo() isn’t static). Passing the factory or factory::getInfo would make that part of the implementation clearer. I don’t think it changes whether the later call is a callback, though.
