### 50. WEE ..EONG `@wyekstudent` (11 posts) 
</div>


<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/277" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**1. :fas-info-circle: Request to help with smoke testing JAR file**
</div>

# Help smoke-test Dingleberry on macOS or Linux

- **JAR file:** https://github.com/wyekstudent/ip/releases/latest
- **User Guide:** https://wyekstudent.github.io/ip/
- **Java version required:** Java 25
- **Operating systems requested:** macOS and Linux
- **Already tested on:** Windows

## Preparation

1. Download `dingleberry.jar` from the latest release.
2. Place the JAR in a new, empty folder.
3. Open a terminal in that folder.
4. Confirm that Java 25 is active:

   '''text
   java -version
   '''

5. Launch Dingleberry:

   '''text
   java -jar "dingleberry.jar"
   '''

## Test checklist

Please check that:

- The JavaFX GUI opens successfully.
- The mascot and styling are displayed correctly.
- The window can be resized without hiding or overlapping content.
- The following commands work:

  '''text
  todo smoke test task
  deadline submit iP /by 2026-09-18 2359
  event consultation /from 2026-09-17 1400 /to 2026-09-17 1500
  list
  find smoke
  mark 1
  unmark 1
  delete 1
  '''

- Invalid commands display a helpful error without crashing the application:

  '''text
  todo
  mark 999
  unknown
  '''

- After closing and reopening the application, remaining tasks are restored.
- The `data` folder is created inside the empty test folder.
- `bye` displays the goodbye response and ends the session as described in the User Guide.

## Results

Please report:

- Operating system and version
- CPU architecture, especially Intel or Apple Silicon on macOS
- Java version
- Whether the JAR launched successfully
- Any failed command or unexpected behaviour
- Complete terminal error messages, if any
- A screenshot of the running GUI

Thank you!
</panel>

<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/73#issuecomment-5438422867" expanded>
