I think they can be seen as logically equivalent. The minimum number of partitions/operands ``alt`` can have is 1, so with only 1, it just means "if the condition is true, execute this fragment. Otherwise, do nothing.", which is essentially what ``opt`` does too, but I feel using ``opt`` rather than ``alt`` for such cases is better since it communicates intent more clearly.
</panel>

