Hello! As a fellow Mac user, this is what I understand:
1. No, it is not expected to run. The `mac` dependency included in the JavaFX tutorial only includes JavaFX for Intel Mac (`x86-64`) and not Silicon Mac (`mac-aarch64`), which is a separate dependency, as you identified. Since your Silicon Mac is currently using the regular ARM OpenJDK 25 installation with no JavaFX installed, it would be unable to run JavaFX, resulting in the error.
2. Therefore, the solution would be to switch to the prescribed `25.0.3.fx-zulu` JDK+FX distribution, which would likely resolve the error you are facing. As you have mentioned, it may not be a good idea to add on additional dependencies that are not specified by the instructions.
</panel>

