I followed the JavaFX tutorial closely up to part 5. I went with a Family Guy themed chatbot interface featuring Brian and Stewie, characters I always see on Instagram reels. I iteratively refined it to match the design I wanted, adding chat bubbles, a themed background and a header displaying my banner for Gnaix. The GUI is connected to the existing command logic rather than reimplementing the task functionality separately.

I found AI useful for getting the JavaFX/FXML structure working and troubleshooting layout issues quickly. Also, to better understand the different styles and formatting, AI was very helpful in guiding me through it. The visual design however required much more manual direction, getting a GUI that looked the way I wanted took quite a few iterations.
