OS: Windows 11
Java Version: 25.0.4

Not sure if its an error on my side, but the app has failed to launch on Windows. I downloaded yapatron.jar from both your release in this post as well as your latest release v0.4 into an empty folder and ran `java -jar yapatron.jar` in PowerShell, but received this error message:

```
PS ...\yapatron> java -jar yapatron.jar
WARNING: Unsupported JavaFX configuration: classes were loaded from 'unnamed module @6b16b98f'

Graphics Device initialization failed for :  d3d, sw
Error initializing QuantumRenderer: no suitable pipeline found
java.lang.RuntimeException: java.lang.RuntimeException: Error initializing QuantumRenderer: no suitable pipeline found
        at com.sun.javafx.tk.quantum.QuantumRenderer.getInstance(QuantumRenderer.java:283)
        ...
Exception in thread "main" java.lang.RuntimeException: No toolkit found
        at com.sun.javafx.tk.Toolkit.getToolkit(Toolkit.java:275)
        ...
```

I tried asking AI for a possible cause and heres the response:
JavaFX couldn't load either Windows renderer (d3d or the sw software fallback). This usually means the fat JAR doesn't contain JavaFX's Windows native libraries, for example because build.gradle only declares JavaFX dependencies for the platform the JAR was built on. It might be worth checking that the win classifier is included for javafx-base, javafx-controls, javafx-fxml and javafx-graphics, then rebuilding the JAR.

I also ran `jar tf yapatron.jar | findstr /i "prism_d3d prism_sw glass.dll"` on my terminal and got `libprism_sw.dylib` only, which is the macOS library.

Since the app didn't launch, I couldn't test any commands. I'm happy to retest on a new build!
</panel>

