<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/484#issuecomment-5728632232" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**5 :fas-comment:**
</div>

`hashCode()` is a method of the `Object` class, and every class implicitly extends the `Object` class.

In the `Object` class, `hashCode()` generates a value based on their memory address, so two different `Remark` objects with matching strings will return different values. By overriding it, it allows two `Remark` objects with matching strings to return identical hashcodes (and thus be considered equal by the overridden `equals` method).
</panel>

