A useful rule could be: a partial PR is meaningful if it reduces uncertainty for the next increment.

For example, a model-only PR is worth merging when its data representation, validation rules, and public methods have been decided, tested, and are unlikely to change once the parser/UI work begins. This lets the next person build against a stable interface.
