### 65. KENN.. JIE `@Kenneth-Chia` (10 posts) 
</div>


<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/253" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**1. :fas-info-circle: Request to help with smoke testing JAR file**
</div>

* Link to JAR file: https://github.com/Kenneth-Chia/ip/releases/latest/download/Sumo.jar
* Link to the User Guide: https://kenneth-chia.github.io/ip/
* Which OS'es to test on: Windows | Mac | Linux

Setting up Sumo:
1. Download `Sumo.jar` from [here](https://github.com/Kenneth-Chia/ip/releases/latest/download/Sumo.jar).
2. Place `Sumo.jar` in a new, empty folder.
3. Open a terminal in that folder.
4. Check your Java version using java -version and ensure Java 25 is installed and in use.
5. Run` java -jar Sumo.jar`

You can try these commands in order:
1. Command: `todo read book`
Expected: Adds “[T][ ] read book”. Total: 1 task.

2. Command: `deadline return book /by 2026-09-20 1700`
Expected: Adds “[D][ ] return book (by: Sep 20 2026 5:00 PM)”. Total: 2 tasks.

3. Command: `event meeting /from 2026-09-20 1400 /to 2026-09-20 1600`
Expected: Adds “[E][ ] meeting (from: Sep 20 2026 2:00 PM to: Sep 20 2026 4:00 PM)”. Total: 3 tasks.

4. Command: `list`
Expected: Lists read book, return book, and meeting as tasks 1, 2, and 3.

5. Command: `mark 1`
Expected: Shows “[T][X] read book” as completed.

6. Command: `unmark 1`
Expected: Shows “[T][ ] read book” as incomplete again.

7. Command: `find book`
Expected: Shows read book and return book.

8. Command: `on 2026-09-20`
Expected: Shows return book and meeting, with their dates and times.

9. Command: `sort`
Expected: Shows meeting, return book, then read book. The normal task order stays unchanged.

10. Command: `delete 1`
Expected: Removes read book. Total: 2 tasks.

11. Command: `list`
Expected: Shows return book as task 1 and meeting as task 2.

12. Command: `bye`
Expected: Shows “Until next time. I'll be here when you need me.” Input is disabled and the window closes after approximately 5 seconds.

At any point of the testing, closing Sumo with `bye` and then reopening it should still result in previous data being saved.
Feel free to report any errors or unexpected outputs,.

Guide for testers:
* Post screenshots from your smoke tests
* Mention which OS you used for testing
</panel>

