<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/163" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**2. :fas-info-circle: Using java vs using CSS to style the GUI background**
</div>



## JavaFX GUI: Setting background image of GUI using Java vs using CSS

**Approach 1 — Java** (in the `MainWindow` controller, which extends `AnchorPane`):

'''java
private final BackgroundSize backgroundSize = new BackgroundSize(
        100, 100,
        true, true,
        false, false
);
Image bg = new Image(getClass().getResourceAsStream("/images/bg.jpg"));
BackgroundImage backgroundImage = new BackgroundImage(
        background,
        BackgroundRepeat.NO_REPEAT,
        BackgroundRepeat.NO_REPEAT,
        BackgroundPosition.CENTER,
        backgroundSize
);
this.setBackground(new Background(backgroundImage));
'''

**Approach 2 — CSS** (painting onto the scroll pane's viewport):

'''css
.scroll-pane .viewport ``{``
    -fx-background-image: url("../images/bg.jpg");
    -fx-background-size: cover;
    -fx-background-position: center center;
``}``
'''

- Java approach is funky, sometimes the image doesn't show
- But I can probably get image to resize automatically every time i adjust the box dimensions
- CSS approach showed the image with no issues but image has scaling problems

Is it more recommended to use Java or CSS for the chat box background?
</panel>

<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/163#issuecomment-5573893979" expanded>
