<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/165" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**2. :fas-info-circle: 💡Delay GUI closing after the bye command**
</div>

If your GUI closes immediately after bye, the farewell message may not have time to appear. 
A simple fix is to display the response first, then use JavaFX’s **PauseTransition** to close the application after a short delay.
```
if (isExit) ``{``
    PauseTransition delay = new PauseTransition(Duration.seconds(1));
    delay.setOnFinished(event -&gt; Platform.exit());
    delay.play();
``}``
```
Replace **isExit** with your application’s termination condition and import the necessary JavaFX classes.

Avoid using **Thread.sleep()**, for example:
```
showGoodbyeMessage();
Thread.sleep(1000);
Platform.exit();
```
As it blocks the JavaFX UI thread, so the farewell message might still not render before the window closes.
</panel>

