<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/405" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**1. :fas-info-circle: Request to help with smoke testing JAR file**
</div>

## 🧪 Smoke Test Request — LittleR

Hellos! Hope someone could help me smoke test my iP

* **Link to JAR file:** [LittleR.jar](https://github.com/LittleLittleLittleR/ip/releases/latest) ([release page](https://github.com/LittleLittleLittleR/ip/releases))
* **Link to User Guide:** https://LittleLittleLittleR.github.io/ip/
* **OS to test on:** macOS and Linux especially, as it has been tested locally on Windows 11 with Java 25, so cross-platform feedback is much appreciated.

---

### Setup

1. Confirm you are on Java 25 with `java -version`.
2. Place the JAR in an otherwise empty, writable folder.
3. Run `java -jar LittleR.jar` from a terminal in that folder.
4. The app should open maximised with an ASCII banner and a welcome message from LittleR.

---

### Things to check

**Basic task management**
* Add a few tasks:
  * `todo read chapter 6`
  * `deadline submit report /by 18-9-2026 2359`
  * `event team meeting /from 19-9-2026 1400 /to 19-9-2026 1500`
* Run `list` and confirm all three tasks appear with the correct type icons (`[T]`, `[D]`, `[E]`).
* Try `mark 1`, confirm the status changes to `[X]`, then `unmark 1` to revert it.

**Search and filter**
* Try `find report` — should return the deadline task (search is case-insensitive).
* Try `on 19-9-2026` — should return the event task only.

**Sorting and priority**
* Set a priority: `priority 1 high`, then `priority 2 medium`.
* Run `sort /by priority /order d` — task 1 should appear before task 2.
* Run `sort /by name /order a` — tasks should be in alphabetical order.
* Confirm the original `list` order is unchanged after sorting.

**Tags**
* Add a tag: `tag 1 2 school`.
* Confirm both tasks show `#school` in the list.
* Remove it from one: `untag 1 school`.

**Edit and duplicate**
* Edit the deadline: `edit 2 /name submit final report /by 20-9-2026 2359`.
* Duplicate it: `duplicate 2 /name submit draft /by 15-9-2026`.
* Confirm the duplicate appears as a new task and starts unmarked.

**Undo**
* Delete a task with `delete 3`, then immediately run `undo`.
* Confirm the deleted task is restored.

**Data persistence**
* Close the app with `bye`, reopen from the same folder, and confirm all tasks, priorities, tags, and completion states are preserved.

**Error handling**
* Try `mark 0` — confirm a red-tinted error bubble appears and you can continue typing normally.
* Try `deadline report /by 30-2-2026` — confirm LittleR rejects Feb 30 as an invalid date.
* Try `event test /from 19-9-2026 1600 /to 19-9-2026 1400` — confirm LittleR rejects a start time after the end time.

**GUI**
* Resize the window to various sizes and confirm chat bubbles expand to fill the available width.
* Confirm commands and `/delimiters` are highlighted in your sent messages.
* Try `help` and confirm the full command list is readable.

---

### How to share your results

* Post a screenshot of the app running (ideally with a few tasks in the list).
* Mention which **OS and Java version** you tested on.
* Flag any bugs or unexpected behaviour you encountered — even small cosmetic things are helpful!

Thanks in advance!
</panel>

