# Smoke Testing
Tested on Windows 11, openjdk 25.0.1.

## Main Tests
- [X] The GUI launches and displays correctly.
- [X] Todos, deadlines, and events can be added and managed using the documented commands.
- [X] list and find show the expected tasks.
- [X] sort orders multiple deadlines by date.
- [X] Invalid input produces a helpful error without crashing the app.
- [X] Tasks persist after closing and reopening Nudge from the same folder.
- [X] bye closes the application.

<img width="344" height="499" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a347d8f3-5487-452d-9847-7e4b0ae07860" />

## Other considerations
To add on to what @chunghean commented, I think sort and event commands can be a bit more flexible.

For sorting, maybe you can allow users to sort base on name as well (e.g. sort /by name), or allow users to choose to sort in ascending/descending order (e.g. sort /desc)
<img width="344" height="184" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/544353db-c4ed-447a-a2c1-c639d954ef52" />

As for adding events, having same date events will be great and it is not that hard of a fix either. In addition, I think allowing users to omit the leading `0` in the date will make the app much more user friendly, as it might not be intuitive to add that `0` when tying out the date.
<img width="345" height="500" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bffb6537-a6f7-490e-b6e2-ed8a71768b76" />

Ultimately, the app runs and checks all the tests you listed. However the inputs quite strict, which may or may not be what you were going for.
</panel>

