<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/554#issuecomment-5891584760" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**10 :fas-comment:**
</div>

My take is that I would not do a separate PR just for an interface change, as nobody can really review it properly without seeing how it is actually used, and it is hard to tell if the method is right until there is a feature calling it.

I think the general practice is to keep PRs small (usually &lt;=10 files) and merge them early, so conflicts do not pile up. The one case where a plumbing PR might make sense is if both features need the exact same new method. Even then, we should include a small use of it so that it is not just dead code.

It might also help to agree as a team on what the interface should offer before splitting up the work, so that you are not changing it every other week.
</panel>

</panel>


