I have managed to get the debugger working by using Remote Development feature on WSL, a feature that the new intelliJ native support was supposed to replace, as a temporary workaround. 

Just to reply to some of the debugging help that had been provided by peers and Prof Damith: 
- I placed the breakpoint when the `execute` method was called by the LogicManager class. However, I felt that that didn't matter since that LoC would only have been executed when an input was given in the GUI, but in my case, the GUI did not even start.
- I had encountered the same issue when trying to use the debugger for my iP (which was also stored in WSL). However, I did not try to run it from Windows. This would be something I would consider when debugging in the future. 
- I had tried to execute the debugger without using Gradle but that did not work either. 
- I had also went through IntelliJ's tutorial on WSL setup, including checking that the package was installed and the setting up of network path. However, based on my understanding, that was meant for running programs that are developed on Windows for testing on WSL, rather than running a program that is stored in WSL. Even so, that did not help in starting the debugger. 

I would recommend anyone else facing the same problem to try out IntelliJ's Remote Development instead. It is quite difficult to debug this issue since there is limited information provided by the debugger. In fact, the screenshot in the original issue post was all that was logged by the debugger and it just continues on in that stage. 
