<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/150" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**2. :fas-info-circle: 💡 Missing Level-10 tag on the dashboard? Check if you actually tagged it**
</div>

If your iP dashboard shows `!Level-10` even though your GUI code is done and merged, it might not be a dashboard bug — it might just be a missing tag.

Unlike the earlier levels, it's easy to merge `branch-Level-10` into master and forget the actual `git tag Level-10` + push step, since by that point you're focused on the GUI working rather than the tagging ritual.

How to check:
```
git ls-remote --tags origin
```
If `Level-10` isn't in that list (even though `branch-Level-10` shows up under `--heads`), that's the issue.

How to fix, if your GUI merge commit is already on master:
```
git tag Level-10 <merge-commit-hash>
git push origin Level-10
```
The dashboard runs once a day, so it won't clear immediately — give it until the next day's run (per the dashboard's own note) before assuming something's still wrong.

Posting in case this saves someone else the same "wait, why is this still red" confusion I had 😅
</panel>

<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/120" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**3. :fas-info-circle: Git-Mastery branch-bender exercise: verify says missing some merges despite all branches being merged**
</div>

Development environment:

macOS
Git v2.39.5
Git-Mastery CLI v7.8.2

What I did:

Working through the branch-bender Git-Mastery exercise (Tour 6, T6L2 — Merging Branches). Per the exercise instructions, I ran:
'''
git checkout main
git merge --no-ff feature/login -m "Merge feature/login into main"
git merge feature/dashboard
git commit -m "Merge feature/dashboard into main"
git merge feature/payments
git commit -m "Merge feature/payments into main"
'''
Expected: gitmastery verify should report the exercise as completed, since all three feature branches are merged into main.

Actual: It keeps returning:
'''
Status: Incomplete
Comments:
- You are missing some merges
'''
Evidence the merges are actually correct:
'''bash
git branch --merged main:

feature/dashboard
feature/login
feature/payments
main

git log --oneline --graph --all:

*   28620a6 (HEAD -&gt; main) Merge feature/payments into main
|\  
| * b307ca6 (feature/payments) Add payments page
| * ce3c962 Add payments script
* |   a532cd7 Merge feature/dashboard into main
|\ \  
| * | 9be78ee (feature/dashboard) Add dashboard footer
| * | 793f8db Add dashboard body
| * | 63a629c Add dashboard header
| |/  
* |   32a580e Merge feature/login into main
|\ \  
| |/  
|/|   
| * 7c3e498 (feature/login) Add login page
| * e7295f8 Add login script
|/  
* 89a6a48 (tag: git-mastery-start-89a6a48) Set initial state
'''
I also tried gitmastery progress reset and re-verifying, with the same result. Is this a known checker issue, or is there something about the expected merge structure I'm missing?

