Tested on:

OS: macOS 15.3.2
Architecture: Apple Silicon (arm64)
Java: OpenJDK 25.0.3 Zulu FX

Downloaded billy.jar into an empty folder and ran java -jar "billy.jar".

Result: PASS — everything worked correctly, no crashes.

Window resize: elements rescale properly.
Overflow + scroll: both mouse wheel/trackpad and dragging the scrollbar work fine once the list overflows.
help and all short forms (t, dl, ls, rm, ?) work as documented, with proper validation messages when args are missing.
Core commands (todo/deadline/event/list/find) and on <date> all work correctly — on filters cleanly to tasks on that exact date.
Error handling is genuinely well done:
delete 99 → clear "no task 99, you have N" message.
deadline x /by 2027-02-30 → correctly rejects the invalid calendar date (Feb 30 doesn't exist) and lists the accepted formats.
An event ending before it starts → rejected with the parsed from/to times echoed back, so you can see exactly what was understood.
bye shows the farewell message, then closes the window cleanly.
Persistence works: relaunching from the same folder showed "Welcome back! Nothing moved while you were gone: N tasks still waiting" with the correct count.

No bugs found. Nicely done overall.

AI disclosure: I used Claude to help plan the test command sequence and draft this write-up; I ran and verified every command myself in the actual app.
</panel>

<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/267#issuecomment-5696141792" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**7 :fas-comment:**
</div>

@robertlivando thank you so much for this — genuinely one of the most useful smoke-test reports I could've asked for. Testing on all three OSes, pasting the full stack trace, and then going the extra mile to suggest the actual fix is way beyond what I expected here.

You called it exactly right: `build.gradle`'s `javafx ``{````}``` block only bundles native rendering libraries for whatever machine builds the jar — I built it on macOS, so it shipped with `.dylib`s only and had nothing for Windows or Linux to render with at all, hence "no suitable pipeline found" on both.

Fixed now with explicit classified dependencies for win/mac/mac-aarch64/linux across javafx-base/graphics/controls/fxml, same idea as what you posted. Also fixed the window-resize issue you spotted on Mac (the ScrollPane was missing `fitToWidth`, so the chat area never tracked the window size).

Verified the new jar bundles 54 `.dll` + 7 `.dylib` + 10 `.so` files (was `.dylib`-only before), and pushed an updated `v0.2` release with the fixed jar: https://github.com/shrad1601/ip/releases/tag/v0.2

Really appreciate the rigour — saved me from finding this out the hard way at grading time.
</panel>

