**9 :fas-comment:**
</div>

Tested on macOS 15.3.2, Apple Silicon (arm64), Java: OpenJDK 25.0.3 Zulu FX.

Downloaded zinc.jar and ran java -jar "zinc.jar".

Went through todo/deadline/event/list (+ls, date-filtered list)/find/mark/unmark/delete, the full contact feature (add/list/update/delete), the ui background toggle, help, error handling, and persistence after reopening — all worked correctly, no crashes.

Findings:

contact list <name> needs an exact full name match — contact list Freddie returns "no contacts found" even though "Freddie Mercury" exists; only contact list Freddie Mercury works. Inconsistent with find (task search), which does partial/substring matching. Screenshot attached.
Duplicate tasks are silently allowed — adding the same todo twice doesn't warn or block. (Also independently confirmed by nje14's Kali Linux test above — reproduces cross-platform.)
Avatar images clip into their border frames — also matches nje14's report, confirmed on Mac too.
Two things nje14 found on Kali that I could not reproduce on Mac: the window has a sensible minimum size (didn't break when shrunk), and an oversized mark number (tried mark 999999999999999999999999) is rejected cleanly with "must be a positive whole number" rather than crashing — screenshot attached.

Solid overall, just those two real findings (partial-name search, duplicates) plus the cross-platform-confirmed avatar clipping.

