</div>

## Smoke test James

**Windows / Linux / macOS testing welcome** · Requires **Java 25**

[Download `james.jar`](https://github.com/jamestorivor/ip/releases/tag/A-Release) · [User Guide](https://jamestorivor.github.io/ip/)

### 1. Launch

Open a terminal in the JAR’s folder:

'''bash
java -version
java -jar james.jar
'''

### 2. Test commands

Enter these **one at a time in the app**, starting with an empty task list:

'''text
todo read book
deadline return book /by 2026-10-15
event school break /from 2026-10-20 /to 2026-10-25
list
find book
list_by_date 2026-10-20
mark 1
unmark 1
delete 2
undo
list
random_sticker
error
bye
'''

Check that the tasks persists after the bye command

Check that searches return matching tasks, task changes work, undo restores the deleted task, and replies, stickers, and errors display correctly.

### 3. Check layout and saving

- Resize smaller/larger: check wrapping, scrolling, and input visibility.
- Close and reopen from the same folder, then run `list`: check all three tasks are saved.
- Capture screenshots of replies/sticker/error, the smaller window, and the reopened task list.

### 4. Reply with this

'''markdown
OS:
Architecture: x64 / ARM64 / unsure
Java: [java -version output]
Result: PASS / ISSUES FOUND / COULD NOT LAUNCH

Checks: [ ] Commands  [ ] Sticker/error  [ ] Resize/scroll  [ ] Saved tasks
Issues: None / action → expected → actual
Screenshots: [attach here]
'''
</panel>

