<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/176#issuecomment-5602279879" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**4 :fas-comment:**
</div>

hi, i don't think the dashboard delay should be the issue because mine always lit up green within one refresh cycle. i am guessing it is because the requirement is that the merged branch is findable in your fork, ie the branch's tip commit is reachable from master. so if you added more commits on the branch after merging, maybe from git's pov, the branch is no longer merged since its tip sits ahead of master? if you are really unsure, maybe wait one more refresh cycle tonight around midnight, else from my understanding, the fix would be just to merge the branch into master again so those commits land there too, and then push both. 
</panel>

