macOS apple silicon
The UI launches cleanly as shown in the user guide. 

Verified working: 'todo', 'list', 'bye' , `deadline`/`event` with tags, `mark`/`unmark`/`delete`, `find` is case-insensitive and correctly ignores tags, tasks + tags + done-state persist across a restart, long unbroken words wrap properly, and mouse wheel scrolling works from launch. Bogos' personality was pretty interesting as well.

`bwhat` is the reply to almost every input error.** `yeet` (unknown command), bare `todo` (missing description) and bare `find` (missing keyword) all produce the identical one-word response, so there's no way to tell what went wrong or what the valid commands are. Your date errors already do this well  using `bwhat [yyyy-mm-dd]`, so it's mostly a matter of extending that pattern to the other cases. Having a `help` list come up upon an invalid command might be helpful.

Also confirming @dillionlim's tag-with-spaces bug reproduces on macOS: `todo spacetag #two words` is stored as `T | false | spacetag words | two`, i.e. description `spacetag words` with tag `two`.
