<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/468" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**1. :fas-info-circle: Request to help with smoke testing JAR file**
</div>

* Link to download the JAR file: [sunny.jar](https://github.com/Vanillajohn/ip/releases/download/v1.0/sunny.jar)
* Link to the User Guide: [Sunny User Guide](https://vanillajohn.github.io/ip/)
* Which OS'es to test on: Windows, Mac, Linux.
* Things to check specifically:
Check if all commands work as expected, as stated in the user guide.
You can try to run edge cases and see if Sunny responds in an expected manner.

If you're willing to go the mile:
1. Deny access to the data dir, by right clicking on it, selecting security, and denying reading/writing access to the user and system. Be careful not to accidentally deny it to the dir the data dir is in. Sunny should tell you that access is denied if you attempt to do a command that writes to the file.
2. Extract the .jar file with `jar xf sunny.jar`, put everything into a dir (e.g. sunnyBroken), delete an essential file/class (e.g. ToDo.class), recompile with `jar cfm sunny.jar META-INF/MANIFEST .` then run the newly recompiled `sunny.jar`.

Guide for testers:
* Post screenshots from your smoke tests
* Mention which OS you used for testing

I had a previous smoke test done for a previous iteration of my ip. Would be appreciated if people can test this again.
Disclaimer: Sunny is meant to be mean to the user.
</panel>

