<panel type="info"  collapsed>
<div slot="header">

### 80. CHUA..RYAN `@ryan24chua` (9 posts) 
</div>


<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/476" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**1. :fas-info-circle: Request to help with smoke testing JAR file**
</div>

Hi everyone! 👋 I'd really appreciate a quick smoke test of **Myriad**, a task-tracking chatbot with a painter personality (your task list is its canvas 🎨). Happy to return the favour.

* Link to JAR file: https://github.com/ryan24chua/ip/releases/latest (`myriad.jar`, v0.3.1)
* Link to the User Guide: https://ryan24chua.github.io/ip/
* Which OS'es to test on: Mac (Apple Silicon) | Linux (I've only been able to test on Windows 11 myself)
* Java version required: Java 25

> [!NOTE]
> v0.3.1 bundles the Apple Silicon (arm64) JavaFX libraries, so it should run on M-series Macs with ARM64 Java. **Intel Macs are not supported** by this JAR.

### Setup
1. Put `myriad.jar` in a new, empty folder and open a terminal there
2. `java -version` (should be 25)
3. `java -jar myriad.jar`

You'll likely see `WARNING: A restricted method in java.lang.System has been called`. This is a known, harmless JavaFX-on-Java-25 message.

* Things to check specifically:
  * GUI opens: painted header with colour stripe, window icon, greeting; the **Paint** button label isn't cut off; window resizes cleanly
  * You can type straight away without clicking the input box
  * Commands work (both Enter and clicking **Paint**):
    ```
    todo read book
    deadline return book /by 2019-12-02
    event project meeting /from 2019-12-02 1400 /to 2019-12-02 1600
    deadline pay bills /by 20/9/2026 18:00
    list
    mark 1
    unmark 1
    find BOOK
    show 2019-12-02
    stats
    delete 1
    ```
  * Invalid input shows a red "Smudge!" error without crashing, e.g.:
    ```
    todo
    deadline x /by 2019-02-30
    event x /from 2019-12-02 1600 /to 2019-12-02 1400
    todo a|b
    mark 999
    list all
    blah
    ```
  * Press ↑ / ↓ in the input box to recall earlier commands
  * Scroll the chat with the mouse wheel / trackpad right after sending a command (no clicking the scrollbar first)
  * `bye`, relaunch, then `list`: tasks are restored from `data/myriad.txt`
  * (Optional) Close Myriad, add a garbage line to `data/myriad.txt`, relaunch: a yellow warning should name the skipped line and every other task should still load

Guide for testers:
* Post screenshots from your smoke tests
* Mention your OS + version, CPU (Intel / Apple Silicon), and Java version (`java -version`)
* If anything misbehaves, paste the exact command and any terminal error
* Suggestions on the UI or messages are very welcome too!

Thank you so much, and good luck with your own iP! 😊


</panel>

<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/341#issuecomment-5726709863" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**2 :fas-comment:**
</div>

**OS:** Windows 11 (x64)
**Java:** java 25.0.4 2026-07-21 LTS (Oracle)
**JAR:** larry.jar from latest release (A-Release)
**Launch:** `java -jar larry.jar` from an empty folder, GUI opened fine

### Works as expected
- Window, custom font and background display correctly; background scales cleanly when resizing / maximising
- Both Enter and clicking Send submit a command
- todo / deadline / event / list / edit / find / on / mark / unmark / delete all behave as the UG describes
- All documented date/time formats work: `18-09-2026 2359`, `20/09 18:00` (year omitted), `1800 21-09-2026` (time first), `2300` (time only)
- `find` is case-insensitive
- Invalid input gives helpful errors without crashing: `todo`, `mark 999`, `blah`, `deadline x /by 31/02/2026 1800`, `edit 1 /by ...` on a todo, `edit 3 /to` before start, `event` with end before start, `delete 0`
- `bye` closes after the intended ~5 s delay
- Tasks, edits and completion status restored after restart

<img width="480" height="565" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/27a568f1-f0b0-4cec-8277-0525cba7a319" />


### Issues / suggestions
1. **Send button label truncated.** It shows as "Se..." at the default window size, and resizing or maximising doesn't fix it. Setting a min width on the button (e.g. `setMinWidth(Region.USE_PREF_SIZE)`) should stop the text being cut off. Even with the window widened, it stays truncated:

<img width="595" height="488" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/459a7080-4ccb-40d4-a1f1-57c291f9fa0f" />

2. **No welcome message on startup.** The chat is empty until the first command. A short greeting would tell new users what to type.
3. **+1 on the scrolling issue, also seen on Windows.** After sending a command, the mouse wheel / touchpad won't scroll the chat until the scrollbar is clicked. This might be caused by `scrollPane.vvalueProperty().bind(dialogContainer.heightProperty())` from the JavaFX tutorial, because a bound property ignores scroll input. Replacing the bind with a listener, e.g. `dialogContainer.heightProperty().addListener((obs, oldVal, newVal) -&gt; scrollPane.setVvalue(1.0));`, keeps the auto-scroll to the bottom and lets the user scroll freely.
4. (Minor, cosmetic) When a task wraps onto a second line, the continuation isn't indented, e.g. "PM)" sits at the bubble's left edge. The task count line in the delete message is also indented differently from the task above it.

Nice work overall, and the custom font and cat theme look great!
</panel>

<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/408#issuecomment-5726978667" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**3 :fas-comment:**
</div>

**OS:** Windows 11 (x64)
**Java:** java 25.0.4 2026-07-21 LTS (Oracle)
**JAR:** themyth.jar from `stable-latest`
**Launch:** `java -jar themyth.jar` from an empty folder, GUI opened fine

### Works as expected
- `quiz` shows a random question; `answer <n>` gives right/wrong feedback and moves to a new question. Option numbering (0-based) now matches the "correct answer" message, so the earlier indexing point looks resolved
- todo / deadline / event / list / list /sort / find / due / at / mark / unmark / delete all behave as the UG describes
- Quoted descriptions work, including commas: `todo "milk, eggs"` survives a save + reload
- Deleting the Quiz Task is refused as documented
- Invalid input gives in-character errors without crashing: `todo`, `mark 999`, `blah`, `deadline x /by 2026-02-31`, `list /sort bogus`, `todo "unclosed quote`, `answer 99` / `abc` / blank
- Found Linus 🙂

<img width="479" height="563" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2510f5e2-e6b1-4f85-ba8f-1f9a114d51e7" />

### Corrupting the save file (`resources\tasks.csv`)
- Garbage line appended / line truncated: the bot names the corrupted file and switches to memory-only mode, and the file is left untouched after `bye`. Nice, no data loss
- Empty file: starts with an empty list, no errors


<img width="301" height="472" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/271e76fd-da7b-4838-afb5-fae3e5835f36" />

### Issues / suggestions
1. **Event can end before it starts.** `event x /from 2026-09-20 /to 2026-09-19` is accepted. Checking `/to` is after `/from` would catch this.

<img width="476" height="563" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/56371e0e-0a09-4333-af91-84d6e31bbb08" />

2. **One bad line discards the whole save file.** With a single garbage line appended to an otherwise valid `tasks.csv`, `list` is empty. Skipping only the unreadable lines (and telling the user which ones) would keep the rest of their tasks available.
3. **UG says closing with X loses changes, but it doesn't.** I added `todo unsaved_task`, closed the window with X, relaunched, and the task was still there. The app is better than documented; the `bye` section of the UG just needs updating.
4. **`find` with no matches says "Found them!"** and then lists nothing (e.g. `find zzz`). A "no matching tasks" message would be clearer.
5. **Input box isn't focused on startup.** You have to click it before you can type. `Platform.runLater(() -&gt; userInput.requestFocus());` in the controller's `initialize` would fix it.
6. **Mouse wheel / touchpad scrolling stops working after sending a command** until the scrollbar is clicked (same issue reported on some other iPs). This might be caused by `scrollPane.vvalueProperty().bind(dialogContainer.heightProperty())` from the JavaFX tutorial, because a bound property ignores scroll input. Replacing it with `dialogContainer.heightProperty().addListener((obs, oldVal, newVal) -&gt; scrollPane.setVvalue(1.0));` keeps the auto-scroll and lets the user scroll freely.

Very fun personality, and the multicoloured text is a great touch!
</panel>

<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/230#issuecomment-5727080695" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**4 :fas-comment:**
</div>

**OS:** Windows 11 (x64)
**Java:** java 25.0.4 2026-07-21 LTS (Oracle)
**JAR:** elora.jar from **v0.4** (latest release; the issue links v0.2)
**Launch:** `java -jar elora.jar` from an empty folder, GUI opened fine

### Works as expected
- GUI opens cleanly on Windows: header, avatar and greeting all display correctly, and the layout reflows well when resizing / maximising
- Both Enter and clicking Send submit a command
- todo / deadline / event / list / find / on / sort / mark / unmark / delete all behave as the UG describes
- Free-text events (`event team meeting /from Mon 2pm /to 4pm`) work and are correctly placed after dated tasks by `sort`
- `find` is case-insensitive; `on` with no matches gives a friendly "Nothing on your list for that day."
- Invalid input shows a clear error in the red-outlined bubble without crashing: `todo`, `deadline x`, `deadline x /by tomorrow`, `deadline x /by 2026-02-30`, `event` with end before start, `event` missing `/to`, duplicate `todo read book`, `mark 999` / `0` / `abc`, `delete -1`, `on 2026-13-01`, `blah`
- Tasks and completion status restored after restart, including changes made before closing with the window's X


<img width="476" height="563" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c532ef00-cda9-42fb-8bf9-5694fe558d84" />

### Earlier reports look fixed in v0.4
- `on 2029-01-02` now shows an event spanning `2029-01-01` to `2029-01-02` (both start and end dates work)
- `sort` orders date-ranged events by start date alongside deadlines
- Impossible event dates are rejected: `event x /from 2028-02-29 /to 2029-01-32`
- No message bubbles spilling over the purple header, even after 15+ messages; they scroll cleanly underneath it

<img width="478" height="563" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/18a6769d-58fb-4917-884e-1f9b478313c5" />

<img width="479" height="562" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/377eee7c-8a1f-49b4-9821-c6168bbe4756" />

### Issues / suggestions
1. **Mouse wheel / touchpad scrolling stops working after sending a command** until the scrollbar is clicked (same issue reported on some other iPs). This might be caused by `scrollPane.vvalueProperty().bind(dialogContainer.heightProperty())` from the JavaFX tutorial, because a bound property ignores scroll input. Replacing it with `dialogContainer.heightProperty().addListener((obs, oldVal, newVal) -&gt; scrollPane.setVvalue(1.0));` keeps the auto-scroll and lets the user scroll freely.
2. (Minor) **Month abbreviation depends on the system locale.** On my machine September shows as "Sept" (`by: Sept 19 2026`) while October shows as "Oct", because Java uses the OS locale for month names. Passing a fixed locale, e.g. `DateTimeFormatter.ofPattern("MMM dd yyyy", Locale.ENGLISH)`, would make the output match the UG on every machine.
3. (Minor) **Date-ranged events show raw dates** (`from: 2029-01-01 to: 2029-01-02`) while deadlines use the friendlier `Oct 15 2026` style. Formatting both the same way would look more consistent.

Really polished app, and the calm purple theme suits Elora well!
</panel>

<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/477#issuecomment-5730850905" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**5 :fas-comment:**
</div>

OS: Windows 11 Home (x64)
Java: java 25.0.4 2026-07-21 LTS (Oracle)
JAR: kaykay.jar from latest release (v0.2)
Launch: `java -jar kaykay.jar` from an empty folder, GUI opened with no terminal errors

Works as expected

* `todo` / `deadline` / `event` / `mark` / `list`: all three tasks appear, the todo is marked done, and dates display as e.g. `25 Dec 2026, 18:30`
* `place add` / `place edit` / `place list`: rating updates from 5 to `4/5` after `place edit 1 /rating 4`
* Invalid input gives helpful errors without adding entries or crashing: `deadline invalid date /by 31 02 2026 10:00`, `place add Cafe /rating 6` (checked with `list` / `place list` afterwards)
* Tasks, places, completion status and the rating edit are restored after closing and reopening the app
* Messages stay readable when resizing the window, scrolling works, and both Enter and clicking Send submit a command

Issues / suggestions

1. `bye` doesn't close the window. After `bye`, the farewell message shows and input is disabled, but the window stays open and has to be closed manually (screenshot below). The UG does mention this, but it's a bit surprising since the app looks "stuck". Closing automatically after a short delay might make it clearer the session has ended, e.g. something like:
   `PauseTransition delay = new PauseTransition(Duration.seconds(2)); delay.setOnFinished(event -&gt; Platform.exit()); delay.play();`

Nice work overall!

<img width="299" height="470" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4e9ceef8-898a-46be-89ad-d5e1c566a248" />
