<div slot="header">

**6 :fas-comment:**
</div>

**OS:** Windows 11 (x64)
**Java:** java 25.0.4 2026-07-21 LTS (Oracle)
**JAR:** wwaffle.jar from GitHub release **v0.2** (the issue links a Google Drive copy; I used the latest GitHub release)
**Launch:** `java -jar wwaffle.jar` from an empty folder, GUI opened fine

### Works as expected
- GUI opens; images, fonts and the music artwork cards all display correctly
- `todo test` → `list` → `bye` → relaunch → `list`: task was saved and restored ✅
- Both Enter and the Send button submit a command
- todo / deadline / event (incl. free-text times like `Monday morning`) / list / mark / unmark / delete / find / sort name / sort status / clear all behave as the UG describes
- Completed tasks are nicely muted and struck through; `find` is case-insensitive and keeps the real task numbers
- Extra spaces are normalised; blank input is ignored; `hello` / `thanks` / `see you` work
- Invalid input gives a clear error without crashing: `todo`, `deadline x`, `deadline x /by 2026-02-30`, `deadline x /by tomorrow`, `event x /from 2pm`, `mark 999` / `0` / `abc`, `delete -1`, `todo a|b`, `TODO shout`, `clear now`, `blah`
- Saves after every change (a task survived closing with the window's X)
- Corrupted `data/wwaffle.txt`: loading fails safely and editing is blocked, as the UG describes. Nice protection against data loss
- `bye` shows the Minion reaction before closing

<img width="476" height="563" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/54c94cd7-e7c5-4619-a347-4ce4bd69f5f7" />

<img width="478" height="563" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b0e13ad1-803c-447f-ae30-e03be20ff0bc" />

### Issues / suggestions
1. **Startup window is taller than my screen.** On a 1280×800 (scaled) display, the window opens with its title bar above the top of the screen and the input box / Send button cut off at the bottom, so I had to maximise it before I could type. Sizing the window to fit the screen, e.g. capping the height at `Screen.getPrimary().getVisualBounds().getHeight()`, or using a smaller default size, would fix this.

<img width="465" height="564" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c0b8dd04-7243-41d9-ba5e-f20ca6e32f11" />

2. **Default Java icon in the title bar / taskbar.** Setting `stage.getIcons().add(new Image(...))` with the waffle image would match the rest of the café theme.

<img width="479" height="563" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a66c9be7-5c06-4e89-b8c8-2ab7f4e3dbbc" />

3. (Minor) **"Welcome back." on the very first launch.** A brand-new user with no save file sees "Welcome back." + "No tasks yet." A plain "Welcome!" when there's no data file would read more naturally.
4. (Minor) **Corrupted-file message could say more.** "I couldn't load your saved tasks" doesn't name the file or the bad line. Mentioning `data/wwaffle.txt` (and the line number) would help users repair it, as the UG suggests.

<img width="478" height="561" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/15701f20-a7ea-49d4-9f42-27f337b3816e" />

5. (Cosmetic) In error bubbles there's a large gap between the ⚠ icon and the text, and wrapped lines start back at the left edge under the icon.

Lovely café theme, and the lyric cards are a really fun touch!
</panel>

<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/502#issuecomment-5740640829" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**7 :fas-comment:**
</div>

**OS:** Windows 11 (x64)
**Java:** java 25.0.4 2026-07-21 LTS (Oracle)
**JAR:** hu9o.jar from `A-Release`
**Launch:** `java -jar hu9o.jar` from an empty folder, GUI opened fine

### Works as expected
- GUI opens with Hu9o's greeting; Enter and Send both submit a command; the dog typing indicator appears
- All core commands work: `todo`, `deadline`, `event`, `list`, `mark`, `unmark`, `find BOOK`, `progress` (1/3 → 33%, then 0/3 → 0%), `delete`
- Lower-case `pm`, `12 PM` (noon) and `12 AM` (midnight) are all handled correctly
- `list please` behaves like `list`; `bye please` is correctly not treated as exit; `hi` / `yo` / `clear` work
- Invalid input gives red error bubbles without crashing: `todo`, `deadline x`, `deadline x /by tomorrow`, `mark 999` / `0` / `abc`, `delete -1`, `blah`
- `bye` → relaunch: "6 task(s) loaded" and `list` shows everything restored ✅

<img width="477" height="565" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8e3b1d9c-e00d-479d-8258-085f26086a5a" />

<img width="479" height="562" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/69d34414-cf25-4814-8098-ff32e82a33da" />

### Issues / suggestions
1. **Event can end before it starts.** `event backwards /from 21/9/26 4 PM /to 21/9/26 2 PM` is accepted. Checking that `/to` is after `/from` would catch this.

<img width="480" height="562" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1dddf5a3-1fbd-426b-b662-3abb1c7a2d87" />

2. **Closing with the window's X loses the session.** I know this is documented, but it's easy to lose work by habit. Saving on close with `stage.setOnCloseRequest(e -&gt; /* save */)`, or after each change, would remove the trap entirely.
3. **Mouse wheel / touchpad scrolling stops working after sending a command** until the scrollbar is clicked (same issue reported on some other iPs). This might be caused by `scrollPane.vvalueProperty().bind(dialogContainer.heightProperty())` from the JavaFX tutorial, because a bound property ignores scroll input. Replacing it with `dialogContainer.heightProperty().addListener((obs, oldVal, newVal) -&gt; scrollPane.setVvalue(1.0));` keeps the auto-scroll and lets the user scroll freely.
4. **Input box isn't focused on startup.** You have to click it before you can type. `Platform.runLater(() -&gt; userInput.requestFocus());` in the controller's `initialize` would fix it.
5. **The typing delay slows things down.** The running dog is cute, but every reply waits for the animation even though the command is processed instantly. A shorter delay (or skipping it for quick commands) would make the chat feel snappier.
6. **+1 on the `h[mm] a` minute form being rejected.** The date error message's own example, `i.e 12/8/26 330 pm`, is itself rejected, so users following the hint get stuck.
7. (Minor) **The UG says the window is fixed-size, but it can be resized and maximised** on Windows. That's great; the Quick start note and Known issue No.4 just need updating.
9. (Minor) **Dates are shown without the year** (`20 Sep, 6 PM`), so a deadline in 2027 looks the same as one in 2026. Including the year, at least when it isn't the current year, would avoid confusion.
10. (Cosmetic) The title bar / taskbar shows the default Java icon. `stage.getIcons().add(new Image(...))` with the dog picture would match the theme. "Now you have 1 tasks" could also be "1 task".

<img width="478" height="563" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/43ef0ce1-849c-40df-876b-aeed5da7070b" />

Cute theme, and the progress bar is a really nice touch!
</panel>

