<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/168#issuecomment-5650858402" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**4 :fas-comment:**
</div>

One thing I found useful was using "planning" mode instead of the regular chat. In "planning" mode, the AI clarified the requirements, and I noticed fewer instances of the AI building what I didn't want.

For larger tasks, such as the iP's GUI conversion, I asked the AI agent to break the work into several commits and suggest commit messages for each. This helped me quickly ensure the planned tasks were completed in increments, making it easier to review the code before committing. I also asked the AI to export the plan as a Markdown file, so if I wanted to work on another PC/laptop, the AI could continue using the context in the Markdown file.
</panel>

