# Panda Testing Guide

<img width="619" height="967" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d33812a2-c24e-42f1-8a19-987c456a0604" />

## Resources

- **JAR:** [Panda](https://github.com/Keegan4/ip/releases/download/v1.0/panda.jar)
- **User Guide:** [View the User Guide](https://keegan4.github.io/ip/)
- **Operating systems to test:** Windows, macOS, and Linux
- **Java version required:** Java 25
## Running Panda

1. Download `panda.jar`.
2. Open a terminal in the folder containing the downloaded JAR.
3. Confirm that Java 25 is installed:

   '''bash
   java -version
   '''

4. Start Panda:

   '''bash
   java -jar panda.jar
   '''

Guide for testers:
* Post screenshots from your smoke tests
* Mention which OS you used for testing

Please complete the following checks:

- [ ] Panda starts without errors.
- [ ] The welcome message is displayed correctly.
- [ ] The command input and Send button work.
- [ ] A to-do can be added and listed.
- [ ] A deadline can be added with a valid date and time.
- [ ] An event can be added with valid start and end times.
- [ ] Invalid commands display helpful error messages.
- [ ] Tasks remain available after closing and reopening Panda.

Thank you for your help!
</panel>

