Yes, I think this would be possible. If multiple methods need to verify the same assumptions about the program state, we could extract those assertions into a helper method (e.g. assertValidState()) and call it where the same assumptions need to hold.
so the code will be something like this:
```
private void assertValidEntry(Entry Entry) ``{``
    assert Entry != null; //Entry should not be null
    assert Entry.getName() != null; // Entry name should not be null
    assert Entry.getId() >= 0; // Person age should not be negative
``}``
```

And i cant seem to find any rules that says it cant, so I guess its allowed. And this also abstracts it out and removes duplicated code
