<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/530#issuecomment-5790036489" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**7 :fas-comment:**
</div>

My understanding is that assertions should be placed where the object is first used, not at the construction of the object. The construction itself should have validation checks to ensure the object is created correctly and does not create from an invalid input, while assertions are used later on in the workstream to double confirm that the object is as you expect and thus behaves accordingly. 

An assertion is not really for debugging but checking that the upstream components or creation are working as intended so that no unintended behaviour is produced and having an assertion at the creation does not meaningfully do that, not to mention it is so close to the construction that the construction itself should already handle such invalid inputs and errors.
</panel>

</panel>


