<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/160" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**2. :fas-info-circle: 💡 [Tip/Fix] Enabling mouse wheel & trackpad scrolling in JavaFX ScrollPane**
</div>

After following the JavaFX tutorial (Part 4), I noticed that the chat window ignores mouse wheel actions over the chat area on initialisation, and is somehow fixed after clicking and scrolling the scroll bar.

In MainWindow.java, the tutorial suggests

```
    @FXML
    public void initialize() ``{``
        scrollPane.vvalueProperty().bind(dialogContainer.heightProperty());
    ``}``
```

However, unidirectional binding (as highlighted in the Javadocs [here](https://openjfx.io/javadoc/21/javafx.base/javafx/beans/property/Property.html#bind(javafx.beans.value.ObservableValue)])) prevents certain properties from being modified - in this case, `ScrollPane.vvalueProperty` from `ScrollEvent`. 

Removing the binding altogether avoids this behaviour completely. Hence, I found this fix to work for me, interestingly also detailed in part 3!

```
    @FXML
    public void initialize() ``{``
        dialogContainer.heightProperty().addListener((observable, oldValue, newValue) -&gt; ``{``
            Platform.runLater(() -&gt; scrollPane.setVvalue(1.0));
        ``}``);
    ``}``
```

This may have a side effect in that new messages will automatically scroll the pane all the way down. 

You can also enable `pannable="true"` on the `<\ScrollPane>` in `MainWindow.fxml` to allow click-and-drag panning anywhere across the chat canvas.
</panel>

