<div slot="header">

**2 :fas-comment:**
</div>

I'm surprised no one mentioned this here, but giving AI the course website URL makes the entire process smoother🥰 You can instruct it to read the updated project instructions every week. This may sound token-heavy, but you won't have to waste as many prompts clarifying instructions or straight up fighting against the clanker. In fact, it frequently highlights stuff that I overlook!

Furthermore, to comply with course coding standards (or even go beyond), you can also get your clanker to scrape the course website or iP pull requests, to summarize the information into the agents.md file. This way, upon starting a session, it will contain all the information it needs to output pristine code. One skill I recommend adding is a git commit/push checker: before committing/pushing, get it to perform a bunch of checks:
- Run/generate additional scripts for code checking, not covered by checkstyle (eg, highlight sus patterns, return file and line number, which the clanker verifies)
- Run automated tests, and on top of that, simulate user testing.
- Highlight all questionable bugs/features to the user.

Happy vibe-coding! Hope my response is genuinely load-bearing.




</panel>

