Personally i think going forward with proper date objects and rejecting old/other string input would be a cleaner way to not only store data, but also allow for date time comparisons in the future, which cant be done using strings. I stored all my dates as LocalDateTime for the Level-8 increment, but i handled for both cases where if a time was given in 24h format as per the example, it would save the date with that specific time. But if lets say a deadline date was given without timing, then it would default to 2359
