Hello! Tested kiwi.jar (A-UserGuide) on macOS 26.6.2 (Apple Silicon/arm64), using Zulu OpenJDK 25.0.3+9-LTS. This is additional macOS coverage; I did not test Windows/Linux. Launched from a fresh folder using `java -jar kiwi.jar`.

All commands in your requested sequence produced the expected results: three correctly formatted tasks, mark/unmark toggling task 1, `find book` returning the todo and deadline, and `on 2019-12-02` returning the deadline and event. `free 4 /from 2019-12-01` returned Dec 04 2019, 08:00-12:00. Deleting task 3 left two tasks, and `bye` closed the window and exited the process. The two remaining tasks persisted after relaunch.

Also checked `deadline invalid /by 2026-02-30` and `mark 99`: both showed helpful errors without crashing. No functional issues found in this limited smoke test. A JavaFX native-access warning appeared at startup, but did not prevent these tests.

