**1. :fas-info-circle: Request to help with smoke testing JAR file**
</div>

Hi everyone! 👋 I’d really appreciate a quick smoke test of **Melodie**, a musical-themed task-tracking chatbot with a doggo mascot 🎵🐶. Happy to return the favour!

### Details

|                     |                                                                                                |
| ------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **JAR file**        | [Download Melodie.jar](https://github.com/Nathaniel-Lim/ip/releases/download/v0.2/Melodie.jar) |
| **User Guide**      | [https://nathaniel-lim.github.io/ip/](https://nathaniel-lim.github.io/ip/)                      |
| **OSes to test on** | Windows and Linux — macOS has already been tested                                              |
| **Java version**    | Java 25                                                                                        |

### Setup

1. Put `Melodie.jar` in a new, empty folder and open a terminal there.
2. Run `java -version` and confirm that Java 25 is being used.
3. Run:

   '''bash
   java -jar Melodie.jar
   '''

Please mention if any errors or warnings appear in the terminal.

### Core features to check

Please focus on these; the User Guide covers everything else.

1. **GUI opens and displays correctly**

   - Melodie’s greeting is displayed.
   - The Mount Fuji background, dog and cat avatars, text, and chat bubbles appear correctly.
   - Commands can be submitted using both **Enter** and the **Send** button.
   - The **Up** and **Down** arrow keys navigate through previously entered commands.
   - Command hints appear while entering commands.

2. **Core commands work**

   '''text
   todo practise piano
   deadline submit report /by 21/9/2026 2359
   event rehearsal /from 22/9/2026 1400 /to 22/9/2026 1600
   list
   mark 1
   unmark 1
   find report
   update 1 /description practise guitar
   delete 1
   '''

3. **Invalid input displays an error without crashing**

   Each command below should produce a red error bubble:

   '''text
   todo
   deadline invalid date /by 30/2/2026 1200
   event meeting /from 22/9/2026 1600 /to 22/9/2026 1400
   mark 999
   blah
   '''

4. **Saving and reloading work**

   Enter:

   '''text
   todo compare A | B
   deadline submit report /by 21/9/2026 2359
   mark 1
   bye
   '''

   Relaunch Melodie from the same folder and run:

   '''text
   list
   '''

   Please confirm that:

   - The complete description `compare A | B` is preserved.
   - The completion status is preserved.
   - The deadline is restored correctly.
   - A `data/Melodie.txt` file is created relative to the folder from which the JAR was launched.

### Guide for testers

- Post screenshots from your smoke test.
- Mention your **OS and version**, **CPU architecture**, and **Java version**.
- Mention whether the GUI opened and whether the four checks above worked.
- If anything misbehaves, include the exact command and any terminal error.
- Suggestions concerning the UI or Melodie’s messages are welcome too!

Thank you so much, and good luck with your own iP! 😊
</panel>

