However, when I entered `event meeting /from 2026-10-01 10:00 /to 2026-10-01 10:00`, the event was successfully added although the start and end times were identical. I'm not sure whether this is the intended behaviour, but I thought I would flag this edge case since an event would normally be expected to end after it starts.

Other than this, all the edge cases I tested produced the appropriate error messages.
</panel>

<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/236#issuecomment-5698166214" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**4 :fas-comment:**
</div>

Thank you guys for the helpful feedback! I’ve updated my chatbot based on your suggestions:

- `list` now displays a clear message when the task list is empty.
- `find` now tells the user when there are no matching tasks.
- When a date is saved as free text and cannot be used for reminders, Yuki now warns the user that the task will not appear in the reminders list.
- Entering `bye` in the GUI now displays the same goodbye message as the CLI and closes the application automatically.
- The User Guide has been updated to explain these behaviors more clearly.

Regarding the following JavaFX warning:

'''text
WARNING: Use --enable-native-access=javafx.graphics to avoid a warning
'''

From what I understand, changing the VM settings on my own computer will not prevent the warning from appearing on other computers when they run the JAR with `java -jar yuki.jar`. Users can avoid it by running:

'''shell
java --enable-native-access=javafx.graphics -jar yuki.jar
'''

However, I have not found a reliable way to include this option directly in a JAR launched with `java -jar`. If anyone knows a better solution, please let me know!

I’ve  published a new release. If you’re willing to help test it, you can download it here:
[Download the latest release](https://github.com/IMNOTANNIE/ip/releases/tag/A-Release)

And I’ve also opened a new request for smoke testing the new version:
[[View the smoke testing request](https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/300)](https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/300)

I’d really appreciate any further feedback. Thanks again for taking the time to test my chatbot!
</panel>

<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/301#issuecomment-5699032663" expanded>
