Tested on Windows 11, Java 25.0.4 with JavaFX.

- Successfully launched using both `java -jar bags.jar` and by double-clicking the `.jar` file.
- The application started successfully, and the GUI was displayed correctly.
- All the features I tested worked as intended.

I really like the animated user avatar — it looks super cool! The `undo` feature is also really useful and a nice addition. However, I noticed a few small things that could perhaps be improved:

<img width="302" height="473" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/233a842f-199e-4610-864f-16c112b62e7e" />

1. As shown in Figure 1, when the start and end date/time are exactly the same, the error message still says that the end date is "early then" the start date. Maybe something like "the same as" or a more general "must be later than the start date" would be a bit more accurate.

<img width="302" height="473" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d7822a38-bfb1-4f2b-93b0-c2991db81dcc" />

2. As shown in Figure 2, I noticed that when I entered a very large year such as `99999999`, the chatbot still accepted it as a valid date. Perhaps some additional validation could be added to reject unrealistic or out-of-range years.

<img width="302" height="473" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/023682ae-4a6e-4426-8f2c-b5d4798637cb" />

3. As shown in Figure 3, when the task list is empty, `list` only displays "Here are the tasks in your list:" without explicitly saying that there are no tasks. This is also something someone suggested to me for my own project. Maybe it would be a little clearer to show a message like "There are currently no tasks in your list." I noticed that your `find` feature already handles this kind of situation nicely!

Other than these small points, everything I tested worked well. Nice work!
</panel>

