I really agree with your approach, leaving a TODO comment is great for keeping the momentum going instead of getting stuck. Building on Prof Damith's point, once you're actually ready to clean it up, you can just highlight that code and ask Copilot or Codex to handle the refactoring for you. It drafts the new classes in seconds, making it way less painful while saving more time. 
