<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/470" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**1. :fas-info-circle: Request to help with smoke testing JAR file**
</div>

Hi everyone! Could you help smoke-test Chim v0.2, my task-management chatbot? It has been tested on Windows with Java 25
 (built targeting Java 25), and I would especially appreciate testing on macOS and Linux.

- Link to JAR file: [[chim.jar](https://github.com/sealfromdowntown/ip/releases/tag/v0.2)](https://github.com/sealfromdowntown/ip/releases/tag/v0.2)
- Link to the User Guide: [[Chim User Guide](https://sealfromdowntown.github.io/ip/)](https://sealfromdowntown.github.io/ip/)
- Which OSes to test on: macOS and Linux in particular; additional Windows checks are welcome.
- Java version required: Java 25 or above. Please check with `java -version`.

Things to check specifically

1. Download the JAR into an empty, writable folder. Open a terminal in that folder and run:

```
java -jar chim.jar
```

2. Check that the GUI opens and remains usable when resized.
3. Try the following commands to add, organize, and find tasks:

```
todo read book
deadline return book /by 2019-10-15
event project meeting /from 2pm /to 4pm
priority 1 high
mark 1
list
find book
unmark 1
delete 2
```

4. Try `mark 99` and `deadline test /by 2019-02-30`. Check that errors are displayed clearly and you can still run `list` afterwards.
5. Type `bye` and check that the window closes. Restart from the same folder, run `list`, and check that the remaining task and its priority tag were saved.

Guide for testers
Please reply with:

- Your OS/version and CPU architecture (e.g. Apple Silicon or Intel/AMD).
- Your Java version.
- Whether the smoke test passed or failed.
- Screenshots from the smoke test, and any error messages or unexpected behaviour (including terminal output if the JAR cannot start).

Thank you for your help!
</panel>

