# Shai v0.3 — Smoke Testing Request

Hi everyone! I would appreciate your help with smoke testing my application, Shai.

## Links

- [Download the JAR file](https://github.com/topinmys/ip/releases/download/v0.3/shai.jar)
- [View the User Guide](https://topinmys.github.io/ip/)

## Operating Systems

Please test Shai on one of the following operating systems:

- Windows
- Mac
- Linux

## Things to Check Specifically

Please smoke test the main features of Shai, especially:

- Whether the JAR file downloads and launches successfully
- Whether the commands described in the User Guide work as expected
- Whether reminders function correctly
- Whether the application handles invalid input without crashing
- Whether tasks remain saved after restarting the application

## Guide for Testers

After completing your smoke test:

- Post screenshots from your smoke tests
- Mention which operating system you used for testing
- Mention any errors or unexpected behaviour
- State whether the tested features passed or failed

Thank you for helping me test Shai!

</panel>

<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/233#issuecomment-5692967595" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**2 :fas-comment:**
</div>

## Smoke Test Results

**OS:** Windows  
**Java version:** Java 25  
**Launch command:** `java -jar beemo.jar`

Overall, Beemo worked well during testing. The GUI, profile pictures, colours, and text displayed correctly. I was also able to add todos, deadlines, and events, use `list` and `find`, mark and delete tasks, and receive clear error messages for several invalid commands. The User Guide also appeared to accurately describe the available commands.

### Issue found: Invalid event dates and times are accepted

The application accepts invalid dates/times and events where the ending time is earlier than the starting time.

#### Reproduction 1: End time earlier than start time

**Command:**

'''text
event midterm /from 2026-09-16 9pm /to 2026-09-16 1pm
'''

**Expected:**  
An error message explaining that the end time cannot be earlier than the start time.

**Actual:**  
The event was added successfully.

#### Reproduction 2: Invalid date

**Command:**

'''text
event CS2100 Quiz /from 2026-02-29 90pm /to 100pm
'''

**Expected:**  
An error message explaining that the date and/or time is invalid.

**Actual:**  
The event was added successfully.

I also tested arbitrary strings, such as:

'''text
event hello /from hello /to hello
'''

These were accepted as valid event dates and times as well.

It would be better to validate that dates and times are valid, and to reject events whose end time occurs before their start time.

