## Test Environment

**OS:** Windows 11 
**Java:** 25.0.4

## Smoke Test Results

Avatars, message bubbles, colours and the input area all render correctly. User messages on the right in blue, Nova's replies on the left in white, errors highlighted in red with a red accent bar. Scrolling follows the latest message and the input field clears after each send.

All eight commands worked as documented:

- `todo Read chapter 6`, `deadline Submit report /by 2026-09-18 2200`, `event Tutorial /from Friday 2pm /to Friday 3pm` — all added, with the deadline nicely reformatted to `Sep 18 2026 10:00PM`
- `list` — correct order and `[T]`/`[D]`/`[E]` icons
- `mark 1` — status changed to `[X]`
- `update 1 Read chapter 7` — description changed and the done status was kept (`[T][X] Read chapter 7`)
- `find chapter` — matched only the todo
- `delete 1` — removed and remaining tasks renumbered

Closed Nova, reopened from the same folder, ran `list`. The deadline and event were both restored correctly. Save file is `data/nova.txt`, with the deleted todo properly gone.

### Invalid input

Tried `invalid command` and `testing123`. Both gave the same error "That command is outside my orbit. Please try another one." with no crash and stayed responsive afterwards.

## Two bugs (agreed to @topinmys [suggestions](https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/417#issuecomment-5729986123) ):

- `bye` prints "Nova signing off" but the window stays open and keeps accepting commands.
- `event read /from hello /to hello` is accepted as-is. Deadlines get parsed into real dates while event times stay free text.

