**Java**: 25.0.4

## Smoke Test Result

`java -jar lily.jar` launched successfully with no error, and `data/lily.txt` was created in the launch folder on first save. GUI renders nicely and it stayed responsive throughout.

Commands worked as expected — `todo`, `deadline`, `event`, `list`, `mark`/`unmark`, `find` (case-insensitive: `find book` and `find BOOK` both matched), and `delete`. Dates render cleanly as `Sep 20 2026`. Invalid input gave a friendly red-highlighted error with no crash, and Lily kept accepting commands afterwards. The tasks were restored correctly from the save file after closing and reopening it.

Nice work!

