### 148. GOH .. RUI `@minrui13` (5 posts) 
</div>


<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/322" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**1. :fas-info-circle: Request to help with smoke testing JAR file**
</div>

* Link to JAR file: [Release](https://github.com/minrui13/ip/releases)
* Link to the User Guide: [User Guide](https://minrui13.github.io/ip/)
* Which OS'es to test on: Windows | Mac | Linux
* Things to check specifically: Test commands and errors

Here is the command summary:
* **Help**: `help` — Displays all available commands.
* **List tasks**: `list` — Lists all current tasks.
* **Sort tasks**: `sort` — Sorts tasks in chronological order.
* **Add todo**: `todo &lt;description>` — Adds a basic to-do task (e.g., `todo read chapter 5`).
* **Add deadline**: `deadline &lt;description> /by &lt;dd/MM/yyyy HHmm>` — Adds a task with a deadline (e.g., `deadline submit assignment /by 20/09/2026 2359`).
* **Add event**: `event &lt;description> /from &lt;dd/MM/yyyy HHmm> /to &lt;dd/MM/yyyy HHmm>` — Adds an event with start and end times (e.g., `event meeting /from 21/09/2026 1400 /to 21/09/2026 1600`).
* **Mark task**: `mark &lt;task_number>` — Marks a task as completed (e.g., `mark 2`).
* **Unmark task**: `unmark &lt;task_number>` — Reverts a completed task back to incomplete (e.g., `unmark 2`).
* **Delete task**: `delete &lt;task_number>` — Deletes a task by its list index (e.g., `delete 2`).
* **Find tasks**: `find &lt;search>` — Finds tasks containing the search keyword (e.g., `find meeting`).
* **Clear tasks**: `clear` — Wipes all tasks from your list.
* **Exit**: `bye` — Saves state and exits the app.

Guide for testers:
* Post screenshots from your smoke tests
* Mention which OS you used for testing

Thanks! &lt;3


</panel>

