<div slot="header">

**2 :fas-comment:**
</div>

I think one practical way to judge this is by looking at the impact of the decision on the rest of the system. If changing the data representation inside Model requires changes to other parts like Logic, Storage, and Ui, then the decision is likely architecturally significant because it affects how all your components interact. On the other hand, if the change can be made entirely within Model without affecting other components, it would usually be considered detailed design. So, the amount of ripple effect a decision has can be a useful way to identify whether it is architectural.

So for your example, the change to Model's internal data representation cascades into three other components, I'd call that a sign the decision was architecturally significant from the start, even if it looked "internal" on the surface
</panel>

