<div slot="header">

**4 :fas-comment:**
</div>

Yeah, CSS feels like the right call here since the background's static. Also you've already got cover/contain/stretch to play with depending on what you're going for. Honestly the scaling "issue" is probably just cover doing what it's supposed to, so switching to contain and slapping a background colour behind it might just fix things without touching Java at all. I feel that you should take the Java route if the background actually needed to change while the app's running, like a day/night theme or something.
</panel>

