# Smoke Testing for Lloyd.jar
- Link to JAR file: [[Lloyd v0.2](https://github.com/Honeybee1011/ip/releases/tag/A-Release)](https://github.com/Honeybee1011/tp/releases/tag/A-Release)
- Link to the [User Guide](https://github.com/Honeybee1011/ip/blob/master/docs/README.md): [User Guide](https://github.com/Honeybee1011/ip/blob/master/docs/README.md)
- Which OSes to test on: macOS | Linux
- Things to check specifically:
  - The application starts successfully using Java 25.
  - Todos, deadlines, and events can be added correctly.
  - Tasks can be listed, marked, unmarked, searched for, and deleted.
  - `check` and `reminder` display the correct tasks.
  - General and command-specific help messages are displayed correctly.
  - The **Up** and **Down** arrow keys navigate the command history.
  - Tasks are saved after closing the application and restored when it is reopened.
  - The window and dialog bubbles resize correctly.
  - Lloyd’s portrait changes appropriately for different responses.
  - Invalid commands and malformed dates or times produce clear error messages.

## Guide for testers

1. Ensure that Java 25 or later is installed.
2. Download `lloyd.jar` from the release page.
3. Place the JAR in a new, empty folder.
4. Open a terminal in that folder and run:

   '''text
   java -jar lloyd.jar
   '''

5. Perform a smoke test using these commands:

   '''text
   todo read book
   deadline submit report /by 20/09/2026
   event project meeting /from 21/09/2026 1400 /to 21/09/2026 1600
   list
   mark 1
   unmark 1
   find book
   check 21/09/2026
   reminder
   help
   help deadline
   delete 1
   list
   '''

6. Close and reopen Lloyd, then run `list` to confirm that the remaining tasks were saved.
7. Try invalid inputs, such as an unknown command or an invalid date, and check that Lloyd displays a helpful error message.
8. Resize the application window and confirm that its contents remain readable.

When reporting your results:

- Mention the operating system and Java version used.
- Post screenshots from your smoke tests.
</panel>

