### 169. ANSO.. HOW `@iians0n` (5 posts) 
</div>


<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/278" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**1. :fas-info-circle: Request to help with smoke testing JAR file**
</div>

Hi everyone! Could you help smoke test **GOAT v0.5**, my task-management chatbot? Testing on Windows, macOS or Linux would be appreciated, especially Windows/Linux GUI feedback.

- **JAR:** [Download goat.jar](https://github.com/iians0n/ip/releases/download/v0.5/goat.jar)
- **User Guide:** https://iians0n.github.io/ip/
- **Release:** https://github.com/iians0n/ip/releases/tag/v0.5

## Getting started

Use **Java 25**. On macOS, use the [course-prescribed Zulu JavaFX JDK](https://se-education.org/guides/tutorials/javaInstallationMac.html).

Put `goat.jar` in a new, empty folder, open a terminal there, and run:

'''text
java -version
java -jar goat.jar
'''

## Things to check

Please check that the complete GUI opens, the text and goat mascot display correctly, and resizing works. Try both **Enter** and **Send**, and check that you can scroll back to earlier replies after entering commands.

Starting with an empty list, enter these commands in order:

| Command | Expected result |
| --- | --- |
| `todo read CS2103 notes` | Adds a to-do. |
| `deadline submit report /by 2026-09-30` | Adds a deadline. |
| `event team retreat /from 2026-09-28 /to 2026-09-30` | Adds an event. |
| `list` | Shows all three tasks. |
| `mark 1` | Marks the to-do complete. |
| `unmark 1` | Marks it incomplete again. |
| `find NOTES` | Finds the to-do, ignoring case. |
| `on 2026-09-30` | Shows the deadline and event; event end dates are inclusive. |

Please also try these error cases. Each should show an error without changing the list or closing the app:

'''text
unknown
todo
mark 999
deadline invalid date /by 2026-02-30
todo READ CS2103 NOTES
'''

The last command should be rejected as a duplicate. GOAT accepts **dates only**, in `yyyy-mm-dd` format; times and natural-language dates are not supported.

Finally:

1. Run `delete 3`, then `mark 1` and `list`. The event should be removed, leaving a completed to-do and an incomplete deadline.
2. Run `bye`. GOAT should say goodbye and close after a short pause.
3. Reopen it from the same folder and run `list`. Both remaining tasks, their statuses and the deadline date should be preserved. The save file should be `data/goat.txt` inside the test folder.

## Reporting results

Please attach **screenshots of the GUI** and mention:

'''text
Operating system and architecture:
Java version:
JAR launched successfully: Yes/No
GUI displayed correctly: Yes/No
Checks that failed, if any:
Additional observations:
'''

If something fails, include the exact command, expected/actual behavior, any terminal error, and whether it still happens after restarting.

Thank you for helping! 🐐

</panel>

