### 172. NG Z.. RAY `@rayyngg` (5 posts) 
</div>


<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/429" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**1. :fas-info-circle: Request to help with smoke testing JAR file**
</div>

Hi everyone! I would appreciate help smoke-testing my TryBot iP.

## Link to JAR file

Download the JAR from the [A-Release page](https://github.com/rayyngg/ip/releases/tag/A-Release) or directly from [TryBot.jar](https://github.com/rayyngg/ip/releases/download/A-Release/TryBot.jar).

## How to launch

1. Download `TryBot.jar` into a new, empty folder.
2. Open a terminal and navigate to the JAR location.
3. Confirm that Java 25 is being used with `java -version`.
4. Run the JAR from the terminal (please do not double-click it): 
`java -jar \"TryBot.jar\"`

## User guide

See the [TryBot User Guide](https://github.com/rayyngg/ip/blob/master/docs/README.md). Type `help` at any time to display all supported commands.

## Commands to test

'''text
help
todo read chapter 3
deadline submit report /by Friday
event project meeting /from Monday /to Tuesday
list
find report
mark 1
unmark 1
tag 1 urgent
tagdel 1
delete 1
bye
'''

Please also check that invalid or unknown commands show helpful errors without crashing, task numbers from `list` work correctly, and tasks persist after closing and reopening the JAR.

## What to report

Please comment with:

- Your operating system and version (Windows, macOS, or Linux).
- Your Java version.
- Whether the JAR launched successfully.
- The commands you tested and any unexpected behaviour or errors.
- Screenshots of your smoke-test results, if possible.

Thank you!
</panel>

<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/128" expanded>
