**1. :fas-info-circle: Request to help with smoke testing JAR file**
</div>

## HappyBot smoke test

- JAR: [[GitHub Releases](https://github.com/EL-NAIT/ip/releases)](https://github.com/EL-NAIT/ip/releases)
- User Guide: [[HappyBot User Guide](https://el-nait.github.io/ip/)](https://el-nait.github.io/ip/)
- Please test on **Windows or Linux** and state the OS/version used.

### Main functionality

Run these commands with future dates:

'''text
todo Review lecture notes
deadline Submit draft /by 2099-12-31 1700
event Team meeting /from 2099-12-30 1400 /to 2099-12-30 1530
list
find draft
due 2099-12-31
mark 1
unmark 1
stats
delete 1
'''

Check that tasks are added, displayed, found, filtered by due date, marked/unmarked, counted in statistics, and deleted correctly.

### Important validation checks

'''text
event Invalid meeting /from 2099-12-31 1600 /to 2099-12-31 1500
deadline Past task /by 2000-01-01
event Ended event /from 2000-01-01 0900 /to 2000-01-01 1000
'''

Check that HappyBot rejects these commands with a clear error and continues running.

### What to report

- Your OS and version.
- Whether the main commands and validation checks worked.
- Screenshots of the application during testing, including at least one successful task command and one validation error.
- Any unexpected behavior or error messages.

Thanks a dozen!!!
</panel>

