**1. :fas-info-circle: Request to help with smoke testing JAR file**
</div>

# Luna Smoke Testing

## Links

* **JAR file:** [Luna](https://github.com/vickylim08/ip/releases/download/A-Release/luna.jar)
* **User Guide:** [Luna User Guide](https://vickylim08.github.io/ip/)

## Operating Systems

Please test Luna on the following operating systems:

* Windows
* macOS
* Linux

## Setup Instructions

1. Download the [Luna JAR file](https://github.com/vickylim08/ip/releases/download/A-Release/luna.jar)

2. Create a new, empty folder.

3. Place the downloaded JAR file in the folder.

4. Open a terminal in that folder.

5. Confirm that Java 25 is installed by running:

   '''bash
   java -version
   '''

6. Launch Luna using the following command:

   '''bash
   java -jar luna.jar
   '''

## Things to Check

Please perform smoke tests to verify that:

* [ ] The application launches successfully.
* [ ] The application starts without unexpected errors.
* [ ] The main features work as expected.
* [ ] The commands and interactions described in the [Luna User Guide](https://vickylim08.github.io/ip/) work correctly.
* [ ] The application remains responsive during use.
* [ ] No unexpected crashes or error messages occur.

## Testing Instructions

After completing your smoke tests:

1. Take screenshots showing the tests you performed.
2. Include the screenshots in your report.
3. Mention which operating system you used.
4. Include your Java version.
5. Describe any bugs, errors, or unexpected behaviour you encountered.

## Test Report Template

### Environment

* **Operating system:** Windows / macOS / Linux
* **Java version:**
* **Luna JAR version or filename:**

### Smoke Test Results

* [ ] Luna launched successfully.
* [ ] Main features worked as expected.
* [ ] User Guide instructions were accurate.
* [ ] No unexpected errors occurred.
* [ ] No crashes occurred.

### Issues Encountered

Describe any bugs, errors, or unexpected behaviour here.

### Screenshots

Add screenshots from your smoke tests here.

Thank you!
</panel>

