<div slot="header">

**3 :fas-comment:**
</div>

If we look at your specific example, changing the internal data representation in Model forcing changes in Logic, Storage, and Ui we can break it down into two parts:

The Internal Choice (Detailed Design): Deciding whether to use an ArrayList or a HashMap inside the Model should just be a detailed design decision. It's an implementation detail.

The Abstraction Boundary (Architecture): The way Model exposes that data to the rest of the system (its interface) is an architectural decision.
</panel>

<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/206#issuecomment-5695697230" expanded>
