minimal Ubuntu installations frequently lack zip or unzip, which leads to silent failures or errors when running the SDKMAN installation script.

If sudo apt install openjdk-25-jdk says the JDK is not found, you can try installing JDK 25 using sdkman, as given [here](https://nus-cs2103-ay2627-s1.github.io/website/admin/programmingLanguages.html). You may need to run sudo apt install zip unzip curl first.
