I agree with @JackChuaYC.

The course website mentioned that:
> **Only merged branches are detected by the script**. After merging each branch into `master`, both the `master` branch and the merged branch must be pushed to the fork.

So the branches need to be merged using `git merge --no-ff &lt;branch-name>`, and then both `master` and the individual branches must be pushed in order for the auto grader to detect it.
