Tested on Ubuntu 24.04 with WSL with the v0.3 release, looks like the date issues with event and LocalDate rounding were resolved. I still found some minor (somewhat edge case) issues:
- Parsing somewhat hostile inputs like a task description that contains the date delimiters eg. "hi/bye" creates an exception for a wrong date format (see the first command that I tried), even if the input date is valid. Might be worth using stricter parsing regex to prevent this.
- Year 0000 is resolved to 0001 in the printout, likely happens from using `"yyyy"` in the `DateTimeFormatter`. Changing to `"uuuu"` should allow year 0000 to be properly printed as such. 

Note on the GUI:
- The scrollbar is kind of invisible being white against a white background.

