- OpenJDK Runtime Environment Zulu25.34+17-CA (build 25.0.3+9-LTS)
- OpenJDK 64-Bit Server VM Zulu25.34+17-CA (build 25.0.3+9-LTS, mixed mode, sharing)

I noted some unintended behaviour for your deletion step once a find has been done. As per the screenshots below, when I ran `find mum` and deleted the first index entry post-find, **it deleted the first index entry off the original list.**

For this issue, perhaps you could consider printing the real indices in find output, rather than making index commands operate on the last result. If you wish to stick to renumbering though, perhaps you could store a mapping from displayed index to real index so you can work backwards from there.

Running with other testcases including persistence did not show any issues on my end. This was verified via the save file in addition to what I see on the UI. My save-file check via `cat data/mouse.txt` shows:

```
T | 1 | none | read book
D | 0 | high | pay fees | 2019-12-02 1800
...
```

Hope this helps!

