# Help smoke-test CHOO on Windows or Linux

Hi everyone! Could you help smoke-test **CHOO v0.2**, my task-management chatbot? Windows and Linux results would be especially helpful because the latest release has already been tested on macOS Apple Silicon.

## Links

- **JAR:** [Download `choo.jar`](https://github.com/ClarenceChoo/ip/releases/download/v0.2/choo.jar)
- **User Guide:** https://clarencechoo.github.io/ip/
- **Release:** https://github.com/ClarenceChoo/ip/releases/tag/v0.2

## Preparation

1. Use **Java 25** and confirm it in a terminal:

   '''text
   java -version
   '''

2. Put `choo.jar` in a new, empty folder.
3. Open a terminal in that folder and run:

   '''text
   java -jar "choo.jar"
   '''

## Test checklist

Please check that the complete JavaFX GUI opens, the CHOO title and avatars display correctly, and the layout remains readable when the window is resized. Try submitting commands using both **Enter** and **Send**.

Starting with an empty task list, enter these commands one at a time:

'''text
todo Read lecture notes
deadline Submit project report /by 2026-09-18 1800
event Team project meeting /from Friday 2pm /to 4pm
list
mark 1
unmark 1
find project
sort
'''

Please also try these invalid commands. Each should show a helpful error without changing the task list or closing CHOO:

'''text
todo
mark 99
deadline Bad date /by 2026-02-30
unknown
'''

Finally:

1. Run `mark 1` and then `list`; the first task should be completed.
2. Run `bye`; CHOO should display its farewell and close.
3. Reopen the JAR from the same folder and run `list`. All three tasks, the sorted order, and the completed status should be preserved.
4. Confirm that the save file was created at `data/choo.txt` inside the test folder.

## Reporting results

Please attach a **screenshot of the complete GUI window** and report:

'''text
Operating system and version:
CPU architecture:
Java version:
JAR launched successfully: Yes/No
GUI displayed and resized correctly: Yes/No
Commands and error handling passed: Yes/No
Tasks persisted after restarting: Yes/No
Checks that failed, if any:
Additional observations:
'''

If something fails, please include the command that caused it, the expected and actual behavior, any terminal error, and whether it still happens after restarting CHOO.

Thank you for helping! 
</panel>

