Here is my Level-10 GUI for CHOO.

<img width="552" height="780" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4fb8732a-7bc0-408d-965b-1e591862e4db" />

I kept the overall chat structure close to Part 4 of the JavaFX tutorial, but added a compact dark theme, styled message bubbles, with original profile pictures for CHOO and the user texting.

AI was quite helpful in helping me explore the different possible designs and implementing the FXML and CSS changes.

However, the first iteration of the AI's design included too much clutter everywhere and made the window unnecessarily wide. The initial font was also too thin, and the user avatar did not fit its frame properly. I still had to manually inspect the GUI, decide which suggestions did not work and ask for several targeted revisions. 

This tells me that while AI was useful for initial implementations and iterations, the final design still required manual judgment from myself.
</panel>

