* Link to the User Guide: https://jyothsana-narendran.github.io/ip/
* Which OS'es to test on: Windows | Mac | Linux (Java 25 required) 
* Things to check specifically:


### Launch Compatibility

1. Download the JAR from the [[A-FixRelease](https://github.com/jyothsana-narendran/ip/releases/tag/A-FixRelease)](https://github.com/jyothsana-narendran/ip/releases/tag/A-FixRelease) release.
2. Confirm that Java 25 is installed:

   '''bash
   java -version
   '''

3. Launch the JAR using:

   '''bash
   java --enable-native-access=javafx.graphics -jar michael.jar
   '''

4. Verify that the application:
   - Starts successfully.
   - Displays the JavaFX user interface.
   - Does not report `NoClassDefFoundError: javafx/application/Application`.
   - Does not fail because JavaFX libraries or native libraries are missing.
   - Does not immediately crash after launch.

### Basic Functionality

Enter these commands in the application:

'''text
todo read book
deadline return book /by 2026-10-05 2359
event project meeting /from Monday 1400 /to Monday 1500
list
mark 1
delete 2
list
bye
'''

The `/by` deadline must use the format `yyyy-MM-dd HHmm`. Event times use a day or date followed by `HHmm`.


Verify that:

- `todo` adds a task.
- `deadline` adds a task with a deadline.
- `event` adds a task with a start and end time.
- `list` displays all tasks.
- `mark 1` marks task 1 as completed.
- `delete 2` removes task 2.
- `bye` exits the application.
- Tasks remain saved after restarting the application.

### Test Report

Please comment below with:

- The operating system and version used.
- The Java version used.
- Whether the JAR launched successfully.
- Whether any warnings or errors appeared.
- Screenshots showing the smoke-test results.

