**Link to JAR file:** [Download ff15.jar](https://github.com/My2h/ip/releases/download/v0.4/ff15.jar) (latest release: https://github.com/My2h/ip/releases)
**Link to the User Guide:** https://my2h.github.io/ip/
**Which OSes to test on:** Windows, Mac and Linux (Mac and Linux especially — I only have Windows)
**Things to check specifically:** cross-platform launch, core commands (tasks and contacts), error handling, and data persistence

### How to run it
1. Put `ff15.jar` in an **empty folder**.
2. Open a terminal in that folder and run `java -jar ff15.jar` (needs Java 25).
3. FF15 should open in a window and greet you.

### Testing
Please refer to the User Guide and choose your own realistic task descriptions, dates, and command order. Interact with FF15 as a normal user. In particular, please check that:

- The GUI launches and displays correctly (title bar reads "FF15 · Assistant to the Regional Manager").
- Todos, deadlines, and events can be added and managed with `todo`, `deadline … /by …`, `event … /from … /to …`, `mark`, `unmark`, `delete`.
- `list`, `find KEYWORD` and `on DATE` (also `on yyyy-mm` / `on yyyy`) show the expected tasks.
- Contacts work: `contact add NAME [/phone …] [/email …]`, `contact list`, `contact find`, `contact delete`.
- Invalid input produces a helpful error without crashing the app (every error starts with "No. GOD. NO." — that's on purpose). Some to try: `mark` with no number, `delete 99`, `deadline x /by tomorrow`, `event x /from 2026-09-20 /to 2026-09-19`, a description containing `|`, adding the same task twice, `blah`.
- Tasks and contacts persist after closing and reopening FF15 from the same folder (a `data` folder should appear next to the jar).
- Optionally: type a nonsense line into `data/ff15.txt`, reopen — FF15 should say which line it skipped and still load the rest.
- `bye` closes the application (the window lingers about a second, then shuts).

### Guide for testers
- Post screenshots from your smoke tests.
- Mention which OS (and Java version, from `java -version`) you used.
- If anything goes wrong, please paste what the terminal printed.


</panel>

