JAR launched successfully: No

Checklist items that failed: all of them — the GUI never opens

Error message, if any:
Error: JavaFX runtime components are missing, and are required to run this application

<img width="796" height="74" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dd2563da-966a-47a3-99f1-a2df980330f3" />

Additional observations:
   `java -jar` cannot work with the current manifest, on any OS.
   Main-Class is stewie.ui.gui.StewieApplication, which extends
   javafx.application.Application. When the main class is an Application
   subclass, the JDK launcher requires javafx.graphics as a named module in
   the boot layer, but a shadow jar unpacks JavaFX onto the classpath
   (unnamed module) — hence "JavaFX runtime components are missing" before
   any of your code runs. This is not platform-specific, so it likely
   reproduces on macOS too if you launch the released jar from a folder
   containing only the jar (rather than via ./gradlew run).
   Prehaps, you can try to add a launcher class that does not extend Application and point
   Main-Class at it as a fix.

</panel>

