Update: I have published a new release, v0.5. The JavaFX GUI now launches directly when running the downloaded JAR file. 

Hi! I would appreciate help smoke-testing my Oreo application.

- Link to JAR file: [Download Oreo JAR](https://github.com/Ken-Tat/ip/releases/download/v0.6/oreo-all.jar)
- Link to the User Guide: [Oreo User Guide](https://ken-tat.github.io/ip/)
- Which OSes to test on: Windows, Mac, and Linux
- Java requirement: Java 25

Things to check specifically:

- The JAR starts successfully using `java --enable-native-access=javafx.graphics -jar oreo-all.jar`.
- The `help` command displays correctly.
- Tasks can be added and listed.
- Tasks can be marked, unmarked, and deleted.
- Deadlines and events can be added.
- The application can save and load data successfully.
- No errors occur because of file paths or operating-system differences.

Guide for testers:

1. Download the JAR file.
2. Check that Java 25 is installed by running `java -version`.
3. Open a terminal in the folder containing the JAR.
4. Run `java --enable-native-access=javafx.graphics -jar oreo-all.jar`.
5. Try the commands `help`, `todo Test task`, `list`, `mark 1`, `unmark 1`, and `bye`.
6. Please post screenshots of your smoke tests.
7. Please mention which operating system and Java version you used.
8. Please report any errors or unexpected behaviour.

### Note on Startup Warnings

The --enable-native-access=javafx.graphics option prevents Java 25 from displaying JavaFX’s native-access warning. The warning does not affect the application’s functionality.

Thank you!
</panel>

