Hi! Could someone help me smoke-test my Bubu JAR on macOS or Linux?

It works on my Windows laptop with Java 25. I would like to verify cross-platform compatibility.

[Download bubu.jar](https://github.com/xinyu-zxy/ip/releases)  
[User Guide](https://xinyu-zxy.github.io/ip/)

### Requirements

- macOS or Linux
- Java 25

### Test steps

Download the JAR into an empty folder and run:

```
java -version
java -jar bubu.jar
```
Confirm that the GUI opens and Bubu's welcome message is displayed.
Then try:

```
todo prepare slides
todo prepare slides
deadline submit report /by 2026-09-18
event team meeting /from 2026-09-19 1400 /to 2026-09-19 1600
remind
list
mark 1
unmark 1
delete 3
mark 99
bye
```
Please confirm that:
- The duplicate task shows an error without crashing.
- The GUI remains usable after invalid input such as mark 99.
- Tasks are still saved after restarting the JAR.
- The bye command closes the application correctly.

Please report:
- Your operating system and Java version
- Whether the JAR launched successfully
- Any errors or failed commands
- A screenshot of the GUI, if possible

Thank you very much!

</panel>

