Hello! Tested on Windows 11. The jar file launched without any issues and the requested items worked as expected:

1. **Functionality of Commands:** help, todo, deadline, event, list, find, mark, delete, and bye all execute properly.
2. **Event & Deadline Time Validation:** Handled invalid deadline inputs cleanly (e.g., prompting for proper date formats on /by today) and correctly created tasks with valid date/time parameters.
3. **Event Date Formatting:** Displayed dates accurately and consistently across task creation confirmations and the list view.
4. **Duplicate Task Detection:** Correctly flagged and prevented duplicate entries (e.g., warning when adding an identical todo).
5. **Profile Picture & Window Resizing:** Avatars (both user and duck profile pictures) remain fully visible, aligned, and unclipped when resizing the window to a narrow view.
6. **Application Exit:** bye command smoothly triggers the closing countdown.
</panel>

<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/371#issuecomment-5711607803" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**4 :fas-comment:**
</div>

Thank you for testing Bubu on macOS and reporting this!

I checked the issue and found that the tasks were not missing from storage. The longer `list` response was being visually truncated by the JavaFX dialog box, which caused the `...` to appear.

I have updated the dialog layout to allow longer responses to wrap correctly. I will include this fix in the next release.
</panel>

</panel>


