### 217. LAU ..MUEL `@sammeowwww` (4 posts) 
</div>


<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/352" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**1. :fas-info-circle: Request to help with smoke testing JAR file**
</div>

- Link to JAR file: [Bob A-Release](https://github.com/sammeowwww/ip/releases/tag/A-Release)
- Link to the User Guide: [Bob User Guide](https://sammeowwww.github.io/ip/)
- Which OS'es to test on: Mac | Linux
- Things to check specifically:
  - Whether the JAR launches correctly from an empty folder
  - Whether Bob creates the `data/bob.txt` file in the correct location
  - Whether tasks are saved and loaded after restarting Bob
  - Whether the GUI is displayed correctly and remains responsive
  - Whether invalid input is highlighted and does not crash Bob
  - Whether the following test cases produce the expected results

## Test cases

Please perform these test cases in order.

### 1. Check the empty task list

Enter:

'''text
list
'''

Expected result:

'''text
Your list is empty. Add a task to get started!
'''

### 2. Add a to-do

Enter:

'''text
todo read book
'''

Expected result:

- `[T][ ] read book` is displayed.
- Bob reports that there is 1 task.

### 3. Add a deadline

Enter:

'''text
deadline return book /by 2026-09-20
'''

Expected result:

'''text
[D][ ] return book (by: Sept 20 2026)
'''

Bob should report that there are 2 tasks.

### 4. Add an event

Enter:

'''text
event project meeting /from 2026-10-01 /to 2026-10-02
'''

Expected result:

'''text
[E][ ] project meeting (from: Oct 01 2026 to: Oct 02 2026)
'''

Bob should report that there are 3 tasks.

### 5. List all tasks

Enter:

'''text
list
'''

Expected result:

'''text
1. [T][ ] read book
2. [D][ ] return book (by: Sep 20 2026)
3. [E][ ] project meeting (from: Oct 01 2026 to: Oct 02 2026)
'''

### 6. Mark and unmark a task

Enter:

'''text
mark 2
'''

Expected result:

'''text
[D][X] return book (by: Sep 20 2026)
'''

Then enter:

'''text
unmark 2
'''

Expected result:

'''text
[D][ ] return book (by: Sep 20 2026)
'''

### 7. Find tasks

Enter:

'''text
find book
'''

Expected result: both `read book` and `return book` are displayed.

Then enter:

'''text
find BOOK
'''

Expected result: the same two tasks are displayed because searching is
case-insensitive.

### 8. Edit a deadline

Enter:

'''text
edit 2 by 2026-09-25
'''

Expected result:

'''text
[D][ ] return book (by: Sep 25 2026)
'''

### 9. Edit a task description

Enter:

'''text
edit 1 description read two books
'''

Expected result:

'''text
[T][ ] read two books
'''

### 10. Test invalid input

Enter:

'''text
hello
'''

Expected result:

'''text
Invalid command :( If you need help, type 'help'.
'''

Then enter:

'''text
deadline submit report /by tomorrow
'''

Expected result:

'''text
Please enter the deadline date as yyyy-MM-dd.
'''

Confirm that:

- Bob does not crash.
- The error response is visually highlighted.
- Bob continues accepting commands.

### 11. Delete a task

Enter:

'''text
delete 3
'''

Expected result:

- Bob reports that the task was deleted.
- Bob reports that 2 tasks remain.

Enter `list` and confirm that these tasks remain:

'''text
1. [T][ ] read two books
2. [D][ ] return book (by: Sep 25 2026)
'''

### 12. Test data persistence

1. Close Bob using the window controls.
2. Start Bob again.
3. Enter:

   '''text
   list
   '''

Expected result: the same two tasks are loaded and displayed.

## Guide for testers

- Post screenshots from your smoke tests.
- Mention whether you tested on Mac or Linux.
- Mention your Java version.
- Report which test case failed, if applicable.
- Include the observed result, expected result, and any error message.
- Mention where Bob created the `data/bob.txt` file.

</panel>

