**Link to the User Guide:** https://yujiankoh.github.io/ip/
**Which OSes to test on:** Mac and Linux especially, I only have Windows
**Things to check specifically:** cross-platform launch, fonts and layout, error handling, and data persistence

## How to run it

1. Put `elsa.jar` in an **empty folder**.
2. Open a terminal in that folder and run `java -jar "elsa.jar"` (needs Java 25).
3. Elsa should open in a window and greet you.

## Testing

Please refer to the User Guide and use your own realistic tasks and dates. In particular:

- [ ] The window opens and the title bar reads **Elsa** with a small portrait icon. The JAR bundles JavaFX natives for Windows, Mac and Linux, but only the Windows ones have ever been loaded.
- [ ] Text in the chat bubbles is not cut off or overlapping.
- [ ] Tasks can be added and managed: `todo …`, `deadline … /by …`, `event … /from … /to …`, `list`, `mark`, `unmark`, `delete`, `find KEYWORD`, `on DATE`, `remind`, `help`.
- [ ] Dates are accepted in any of `2019-10-15`, `15/10/2019`, `Oct 15 2019`, `October 15 2019`, and are always shown back as `Oct 15 2019`.
- [ ] Bad input gives a helpful message instead of crashing. Some to try: `blah`, `mark` with no number, `delete 99`, `deadline x /by tomorrow`, `event x /from 2026-09-20 /to 2026-09-19`, the same `todo` twice, `deadline x /by 1/1/2026 /by 2/2/2026`.
- [ ] Errors are shown in a **pink bubble with a bar down the left edge**, distinct from normal replies.
- [ ] The profile pictures are circular, not square.
- [ ] Tasks persist: add some, `bye`, reopen from the same folder. A `data` folder should appear **next to the jar**.

Guide for testers:
* Post screenshots from your smoke tests
* Mention which OS and Java version (`java -version`) you used
* If anything goes wrong, please paste what the terminal printed


