 Tested on macOS 15.6.1 (Apple Silicon), OpenJDK 25.0.2 (ARM64).

  Launch issue: Running java -jar larry.jar fails before the window opens. The bundled JavaFX native libraries are x86_64, but ARM64 Java requires arm64. The errors include incompatible architecture and No toolkit
  found.

  Using separate ARM64 JavaFX 17.0.7 libraries with the unchanged JAR, the following passed:

  - Interface, custom font, background, and messages displayed correctly.
  - Adding, listing, editing, finding, marking, unmarking, and deleting tasks.
  - Documented date/time formats, including omitted years and time-only input.
  - Saved tasks, edits, and completion status restored after restart; deleted tasks remained deleted.
  - Invalid commands produced helpful errors without crashing.
  - Both Enter and Send submitted commands.

  Invalid inputs tested included todo, mark 999, and deadline invalid /by 31/02/2026 1800.

  The main issue is out-of-the-box compatibility with ARM64 Java on Apple Silicon. 

  
