### 247. DANI..IANG `@itsDanielGuan` (3 posts) 
</div>


<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/450" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**1. :fas-info-circle: Specification of Callback functions**
</div>

<img width="600" height="400" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/95ad9fc6-97ee-48c7-a4a4-14e3bcc861f6" />

Hi Everyone,

This question was shown during the tutorial. I think that there is some ambiguity when it comes to whether getInfo() is a callback function. There is the possibility that getInfo() is just a public method that the Parser object can access directly, which should not be considered a callback. I think a more accurate representation is to have the ParserFactory object call Parser(getInfo) to explicitly pass the callback function to the Parser object. What do you think? Happy to hear your thoughts.



</panel>

<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/76#issuecomment-5448169422" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**2 :fas-comment:**
</div>

I prefer composition with `List&lt;Task>` being a field in `TaskList`. Direct extension meant that it exposed all the methods that may not be relevant to `TaskList`. Easier to have greater control over exactly which operations are required for the class.
</panel>

