**1. :fas-info-circle: [RepoSense] What do the ramp colors represent?**
</div>

**Question: What do the ramp colors represent?**

I'm trying to understand how RepoSense assigns colors to commit ramps.

Excerpt from the RepoSense User Guide:
<img width="700" height="41" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/97579f02-bacc-4f38-98f3-c270cd0df36d" />

My interpretation so far:
Each day's commits are assigned a distinct color. For example, Aug 25 = yellow, Aug 26 = light blue, Aug 27 = dark green, and so on.

What I'm confused about:
This interpretation breaks down when I look at the example below, where there are two separate orange commits, one falling within Aug 25 and another within Aug 26:

<img width="428" height="56" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8fe8dd71-a31d-44ca-8fdd-88be66a228ae" />

(Sorry for using your commits as an example, it looks colorful!)

If color maps 1:1 to day, shouldn't each day only ever show one color? Why would orange appear across two different days?
Does anyone know what's actually assigning the colors here?

Thank you in advance for sharing your insights. 😊


</panel>

