# Help smoke-test Pebby on Windows or Linux

Hi everyone! Could you help smoke-test **Pebby v0.2**, my task-management chatbot? Windows and Linux results would be especially helpful.

## Links

- **JAR:** [Download `pebby.jar`](https://github.com/0218hy/ip/releases/download/v0.2/pebby.jar)
- **User Guide / repository:** [https://github.com/0218hy/ip](https://github.com/0218hy/ip)
- **Release:** [https://github.com/0218hy/ip/releases/tag/v0.2](https://github.com/0218hy/ip/releases/tag/v0.2)

## Preparation

1. Use **Java 25** and confirm it in a terminal:

   '''text
   java -version
   '''

2. Put `pebby.jar` in a new, empty folder.
3. Open a terminal in that folder and run:

   '''text
   java -jar "pebby.jar"
   '''

## Test checklist

Please check that the complete JavaFX GUI opens, the Pebby title and avatars display correctly, and the layout remains readable when the window is resized. Try submitting commands using both **Enter** and **Send**.

Starting with an empty task list, enter these commands one at a time:
- [ ] todo Read lecture notes
- [ ] deadline Submit project report /by 2026-09-18
- [ ] event Team project meeting /from 2026-09-17 /to 2026-09-18
- [ ] list
- [ ] mark 1
- [ ] unmark 1
- [ ] find project
- [ ] schedule 2026-09-18


Please also try these invalid commands. Each should show a helpful error without changing the task list or closing Pebby:
- [ ] todo
- [ ] mark 99
- [ ] deadline Bad date /by 2026-02-30
- [ ] event Invalid dates /from 2026-09-20 /to 2026-09-18
- [ ] unknown



Finally:

1. Run `mark 1` and then `list`; the first task should be completed.
2. Run `bye`; Pebby should close.
3. Reopen the JAR from the same folder and run `list`. All three tasks and the completed status should be preserved.
4. Confirm that the save file was created at `data/pebby.txt` inside the test folder.

## Reporting results

Please attach a **screenshot of the complete GUI window** and report:

'''text
Operating system and version:
JAR launched successfully: Yes/No
GUI displayed and resized correctly: Yes/No
Commands and error handling passed: Yes/No
Tasks persisted after restarting: Yes/No
Checks that failed, if any:
Additional observations:
'''

If something fails, please include the command that caused it, the expected and actual behaviour, any terminal error, and whether it still happens after restarting Pebby.

Thank you for helping! 🪨

<img width="1468" height="838" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/876d67e3-77a9-499b-a5c2-1f307e8fd7a4" />

</panel>

