## Request for help with smoke testing Sophon JAR

Hi everyone! I’m looking for help smoke-testing the packaged JAR file for my iP, especially on different operating systems.

### Links

- **JAR file:** [[Download sophon.jar](https://github.com/herohelennn1010/ip/releases/latest/download/sophon.jar)](https://github.com/herohelennn1010/ip/releases/latest/download/sophon.jar)
- **User Guide:** [[Sophon User Guide](https://herohelennn1010.github.io/ip/)](https://herohelennn1010.github.io/ip/)

### Operating systems to test

- Windows
- macOS, including Apple Silicon if available
- Linux

### Requirements

Please install **Java 25** and confirm the installed version by running:

'''text
java -version
'''

Download `sophon.jar`, open a terminal in its folder, and run:

'''text
java -jar sophon.jar
'''

### Things to check

Please check whether:

- The application starts successfully without a fatal error.
- The window title is `Sophon · Deep Space Interface`.
- The title, subtitle, input box, **TRANSMIT** button, scrollbar, messages, and avatars display correctly.
- Text is readable and does not overlap, disappear, or get cut off.
- Long messages wrap correctly.
- Pressing Enter and clicking **TRANSMIT** both submit a command.
- The conversation scrolls to the newest message after several commands.
- Earlier messages remain accessible using the scrollbar.
- The application remains responsive after multiple commands.
- Closing and reopening the application preserves saved tasks.
- Entering `bye` displays the farewell message, disables further input, and closes the window after approximately three seconds.

Please try the following commands:

'''text
todo read a book
deadline return book /by 2026-10-15
event school break /from 2026-10-20 /to 2026-10-25
list
find book
mark 1
unmark 1
delete 2
list
'''

Please also enter an invalid command such as:

'''text
nonsense
'''

Check that Sophon displays a clear response and remains usable afterward.

### Guide for testers

When replying, please include:

- Your operating system and version
- Your CPU architecture, such as Intel x64, AMD64, or Apple Silicon
- Your Java version
- Screenshots of the application during the smoke test
- Whether startup, commands, scrolling, exit behavior, and persistence worked
- Any broken images, layout problems, unreadable or truncated text, unexpected command behavior, or startup errors
- Any warnings printed in the terminal

Example environment information:

'''text
OS: Windows 11
Architecture: Intel x64
Java: 25.0.4.1
Result: Passed / Issues found
'''

Thank you for helping me test Sophon!
</panel>

