### 268. RAJK..SHNU `@vishnuroxx` (3 posts) 
</div>


<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/502" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**1. :fas-info-circle: Request to help with smoke testing JAR file**
</div>

Hi everyone! 👋 I'd really appreciate a quick smoke test of **Hu9o**, a task-tracking chatbot with a dog for a mascot 🐶 (it also keeps a small contacts book, but that's not needed for this test). Happy to return the favour!

### Details

| | |
|---|---|
| **JAR file** | [hu9o.jar](https://github.com/vishnuroxx/ip/releases/tag/A-Release) |
| **User Guide** | https://vishnuroxx.github.io/ip/ |
| **OSes to test on** | Mac, Windows and Linux |
| **Java version** | Java 25 |

### Setup

1. Put `hu9o.jar` in a new, empty folder and open a terminal there
2. Run `java -version` (should be 25)
3. Run `java -jar hu9o.jar`

> **Note:** You'll likely see `WARNING: A restricted method in java.lang.System has been called`. This is a known, harmless JavaFX-on-Java-25 message.

### Core features to check

Please stick to these; the User Guide covers everything else.

1. **GUI opens** with Hu9o's greeting, and you can send commands with both **Enter** and the **Send** button. A small animated dog appears briefly while Hu9o "types" each reply.

2. **Core commands work:**
   ```
   todo read book
   deadline return book /by 20/9/26 6 PM
   event project meeting /from 20/9/26 2 PM /to 20/9/26 4 PM
   list
   mark 1
   unmark 1
   find BOOK
   progress
   delete 1
   ```

3. **Invalid input shows a red error bubble without crashing:**
   ```
   todo
   deadline x /by tomorrow
   mark 999
   blah
   ```

4. **Saving works:** type `bye`, then relaunch from the same folder and run `list`. Your tasks should be restored.

> **Important:** Please exit with `bye`, not the window's close button. Hu9o only saves on `bye`.

### Guide for testers

- Post screenshots from your smoke tests
- Mention your **OS + version**, **CPU** (Intel / Apple Silicon), and **Java version** (`java -version`)
- If anything misbehaves, paste the exact command and any terminal error
- Suggestions on the UI or messages are very welcome too!

Thank you so much, and good luck with your own iP! 😊

</panel>

<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/451#issuecomment-5729994517" expanded>
