### 273. CHAW..XUAN `@YourHand29` (3 posts) 
</div>


<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/232" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**1. :fas-info-circle: Request to help with smoke testing JAR file**
</div>

## Smoke Testing Request

Hi everyone! I would appreciate help smoke-testing my iP, **YourHand**, on macOS and Linux.

- Link to JAR file: [Download JAR File](https://github.com/YourHand29/ip/releases/download/A-Release-v0.2/yourhand.jar)
- Link to User Guide: [View User Guide](https://yourhand29.github.io/ip/)
- OSes to test on: macOS | Linux

### What to test

Please check that:

1. The JAR launches successfully with Java 25 using:
   '''bash
   java -version
   java -jar yourhand.jar
   '''
2. The GUI opens correctly and displays the YourHand header, welcome message, task area, input box, and **Send** button.
3. The following commands work:
   - `help`
   - `todo read lecture notes`
   - `deadline submit report /by 2026-10-01`
   - `event team meeting /from 2026-09-20 1400 /to 2026-09-20 1500`
   - `list`
   - `find report`
   - `view schedule 2026-09-20`
   - `mark 1`
   - `unmark 1`
   - `delete 1`
4. Invalid commands produce a helpful error without crashing the application.
5. Tasks are still present after closing and reopening the JAR.
6. The application can be closed normally using `bye`.

### Important smoke-test setup

Please copy only the JAR file into a new, empty folder before testing. This helps identify hard-coded file paths and storage issues.

### Guide for testers

- Please test the JAR from a terminal rather than double-clicking it.
- Please post screenshots of your smoke-test results, especially the launch screen and a successful command flow.
- I have currently smoke-tested the application only on Windows, as that is the only OS available to me. Testing on macOS or Linux would help verify cross-platform compatibility.

Please report your OS, Java version, commands tested, and any errors encountered. Thank you!



</panel>

