- x86-64 (AMD Ryzen 9 7940HS)
- `java -version`: `25.0.4 2026-07-21 LTS`, HotSpot 64-Bit Server VM `25.0.4+7-LTS-189`
- Ran `java -jar ip.jar` from an empty folder, without renaming it

**What passed**

1. GUI opens on Java 25, greeting shows, fresh folder starts empty.
2. `todo`, `deadline ... /by 2026-09-20` and `event ... /from ... /to ...` all added, and `list` shows them in the formats given in your guide.
3. `mark 2`, `unmark 2` and `delete 3` work. `find proj rep` matched `Submit project report`, so partial words, keyword order and case are all handled, and the search results use their own numbering as documented.
4. Bad input, none of which crashed it:
   - `blah` gives "that order is unclear"
   - `todo` with no description states the format
   - `deadline Pay bills /by 20 Sep 2026` states the format
   - `event Trip /from 2026-09-21 /to 2026-09-21` and a reversed range are both rejected with "the event end date must be after its start date"
   - `todo   READ a BOOK  ` was rejected as a duplicate and said which task it matched
   - `mark 99`, `mark abc`, `delete 0` and `find` with no keyword all give a clear message
5. `LIST` in caps works, and `todo 读一本书` added and listed correctly.
6. Help button works and kept my unfinished `todo half typed command` in the input box. Send button and Enter both submit. The box only clears when the command succeeds.
7. Scrolling works and the view follows the newest message. The window has a minimum size of about 525x650. At the minimum the header subtitle drops out and the bubbles wrap, and at 1150 wide a "Captain Cutter" chip appears in the header. Nothing overlapped or got cut off at any size I tried.
8. `bye` closed the window. `data/serina.txt` was created in the folder I launched from. Reopening from the same folder brought back all four tasks with the completed one still marked `[X]`.

I also edited line 2 of `data/serina.txt` to make it invalid and restarted. It warned "Invalid record on line 2", blocked task commands, left `help` and `bye` working, and did not overwrite the file. That matches what your guide says it should do.

I did not test the 100 task cap.

**Two small things**

1. `deadline Pay bills /by 2026-02-30` replies that I should use `yyyy-MM-dd`. That was already the format I used. The actual problem is that February has no 30th, so the message points at the wrong thing. Your guide lists `2026-02-30` as a rejected case, so it would help to say something like "2026-02-30 is not a real date" instead.

2. Resizing the window leaves the chat at the same scroll position instead of going back to the newest message. To reproduce: send a command so the view sits at the bottom, then drag the window narrower. The content reflows taller and you end up part way up the history. Cosmetic only, and it does not come up in normal use.

