* Which OS'es to test on: Windows, Mac and Linux
* Things to check specifically: Cross-platform launch, core commands (including updating), error handling, and data persistence

## Testing
Please refer to the User Guide and choose your own realistic task descriptions, dates, and command order. Feel free to interact with Bob as a normal user. In particular, please check that:

* The GUI launches and displays correctly.
* Todos, deadlines, and events can be added and managed using the documented commands.
* list and find show the expected tasks.
* update changes the details accordingly.
* Invalid input produces a helpful error without crashing the app.
* Tasks persist after closing and reopening Nudge from the same folder.
* bye closes the application.


Guide for testers:
* Post screenshots from your smoke tests
* Mention which OS you used for testing


</panel>

<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/73#issuecomment-5436942055" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**2 :fas-comment:**
</div>

I agree with the rest that treating the non-date time entries as invalid and skipping them on load, as setting dates to LocalDateTime also imparts specific meaning that might need to be used later on, such as day of week, or even ordering (e.g. order events and deadlines by ascending order). Trying to parse old data would mean giving these data meaning that might not have been intended.
</panel>

</panel>


