Yea if we name every literal, then the code is gonna be more confusing that it should be... E.g. if it's a simple loop that we just want to run 3 times, it might make more sense to hardcode "3" rather than obfuscate it with a "LOOP_COUNT" var - which will require me to look at the LOOP_COUNT var in order to know it's value 3..

So it's discretionary imo - can't just blindly follow the requirements
