Thanks @zRayhhh, tried your workaround and it seems to fix the UI bug on SceneBuilder.

Just wanted to add: for others using the workaround, if the second `mvnw package ...` rebuild command fails due to missing dependency (as `app` depends on both `kit` and `gluon-plugin`), you can try using the following to install both dependencies.
```
./mvnw clean install -pl app -am -DskipTests
```
Then, launch the wrapper as mentioned in the above workaround.
```
./mvnw javafx:run -f app
```
