<img width="520" alt="List after restarting the app" src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Lew1sWong/forum-smoke-tests/main/meowmeow-2-after-restart.png" />

</panel>

<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/514#issuecomment-5758530488" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**2 :fas-comment:**
</div>



Tested on **macOS 27.0 (Apple silicon, M5)** with **Zulu OpenJDK 25.0.3**, run from an empty folder with `java -jar trackie.jar`. The reports above are all Windows 11, so here's a macOS data point — noting you asked for Windows/Linux, so treat this as a bonus rather than the coverage you wanted.

**Working as intended**

- Launches straight from `java -jar`, title bar shows "Trackie". The only console output is the usual JavaFX `--enable-native-access` warning that Java 24+ prints for every JavaFX app — harmless.
- All four task types add and list correctly (`todo` / `deadline` / `event` / `within`), and the "Now you have N tasks" count stayed consistent throughout.
- `mark`, `unmark`, `find` and `delete` all behaved as expected.
- No invalid command closed the app. Unknown command, bare `todo`, `deadline` without `/by`, `mark 99`, `mark abc` and `delete 0` each produced a clear red error bubble. `mark abc` giving "The task number must be a whole number" and `mark 99` giving "Choose a task number between 1 and 3" are both nicely specific.
- `bye` closed the window cleanly and relaunching restored the saved tasks.
- Resizing is fine. You've set a 500x400 minimum so the layout can't be squashed, and it stays correct when widened — sensible choice.
- Two things I tried to break and couldn't, both worth calling out: a description containing `|` is explicitly rejected ("Task descriptions cannot contain the | character"), which protects your pipe-delimited save file; and non-ASCII descriptions (I used Chinese) survive a save/reload round trip intact.

**Two small issues**

1. **`find` is case-sensitive.** With a task `submit project report` in the list, `find report` matches it but `find REPORT` returns nothing. Lowercasing both the keyword and the description before comparing would make this less surprising.

2. **An empty `find` result shows only the header.** When nothing matches, the reply is just "Here's what I found on the trail:" with nothing underneath, which reads like the app did nothing rather than like a deliberate "no matches". A "no matching tasks" line would make it unambiguous. Screenshot 4 shows both issues in one run — `find report` hits, `find REPORT` and `find zzzzz` both come back as a bare header.

Also — I can confirm @irtan-cell's observation on macOS: the `deadline` error message says `/by TIME` while the app only accepts a date.

Nice work overall, it's a polished app and the error handling is more thorough than most.

---

*Disclosure: I used Claude Code to script these runs — it drove the JavaFX window directly (typing into `#userInput` and firing the action) so every run is reproducible from a clean folder. The findings above are read off the resulting screenshots and the on-disk `data/trackie.txt`, both of which are included here so you can check them against your own build.*

