### Quiz functionality works

- command `quiz` → shows randomised quiz question
- command `answer <Integer>` with the correct answer → shows a success message and marks quiz task as complete
- command `answer <Integer>` with the wrong answer → shows a message with the correct answer instead

> [!TIP]
> The answer choices displayed with the question are zero-indexed but when the correct answer is shown after the user types the incorrect answer, it is one-indexed. It would be less confusing if they both followed the same indexing.

