## macOS smoke test — Aegis v0.2

**Environment:** macOS 15.6.1 (Apple Silicon, arm64); Azul Zulu OpenJDK 25.0.3. I downloaded the linked release JAR into an empty folder and launched it with `java -jar aegis.jar`.


<img width="417" height="600" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/21afc747-9005-4ed3-a29e-482c5f962e19" />


**Results:**

- The JavaFX window opened without a missing-library error or crash. The chat text, avatars, input field, and Send button rendered clearly in the captured view.
- Added `todo buy milk`, `deadline submit report /by 2026-09-25`, and `event project meeting /from 2026-09-20 /to 2026-09-21`. `list` showed all three with the expected descriptions and dates.
- `mark 1` changed the todo to `[X]`; `unmark 1` changed it back to `[ ]`. `find report` returned the deadline.
- `sort` reordered the list to event (Sep 20), deadline (Sep 25), then the undated todo. A second `todo buy milk` was rejected as a duplicate. `delete 3` removed that todo, and the following `list` contained only the event and deadline.
- A fresh launch from the same folder restored those two remaining tasks from `data/aegis.txt`.

No functional issue surfaced in these checks. The terminal printed the JavaFX restricted native-access warning at startup, but the app continued normally. Commands were submitted through the GUI input field's action event; physical keyboard, mouse, and scrolling were not covered.

</panel>

<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/295#issuecomment-5698140197" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**2 :fas-comment:**
</div>

## macOS smoke test — Elsa v2.0

**Environment:** macOS 15.6.1 (Apple Silicon, arm64); Azul Zulu OpenJDK 25.0.3. I downloaded the linked release JAR into an empty folder and launched it with `java -jar elsa.jar`.

<img width="520" height="640" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/df5edd5e-c5ef-4668-969c-0c50ed9664c5" />

**Results:**

- The JavaFX window opened without a missing-library error or crash. The chat bubbles, avatars, input field, and Send button rendered clearly in the captured GUI view. Error replies were pink with a left bar, as described in the request.
- Added `todo buy milk`, `deadline submit report /by 2026-09-25`, and `event project meeting /from 2026-09-20 /to 2026-09-21`. `list` showed all three with correctly formatted dates.
- `mark 1` changed the todo to `[X]`; `unmark 1` changed it back to `[ ]`. `find report` found the deadline. `on 2026-09-20` found the event; `remind` and `help` returned normal responses.
- `blah`, `mark`, `delete 99`, `deadline x /by tomorrow`, and an event ending before it starts all produced helpful error replies. Adding `todo buy milk` a second time was rejected, and a subsequent `list` still showed exactly three tasks.
- `data/elsa.txt` was created. On a fresh launch from the same folder, the three tasks were restored; attempts to add them again were rejected as duplicates.

No functional issue surfaced in these checks. The terminal printed the JavaFX restricted native-access warning at startup, but the app continued normally. Commands were submitted through the GUI input field's action event; physical keyboard, mouse, scrolling, alternate date formats, `bye`, and window-close behavior were not covered.

