### 355. LINU.. JIN `@Linux735` (1 posts) 
</div>


<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/73#issuecomment-5437375699" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**1 :fas-comment:**
</div>

I agree with most others that the now invalid entry can be safely ignored in our case, given the project requirements. For me I had designed my parsing of the save file to handle and skip invalid/corrupted entries and continue loading the rest of the file as required. When I encountered the error myself I simply deleted/reset my data.txt file that was storing the entries as a 1 time fix. In my opinion, it would be way too much effort to support the migration of existing tasks with a wrong date format as we originally had no real restriction on what a user could input and there would be way too many cases to manage. Perhaps an error message could be presented to the user upon the one time change to inform them that a task has been deleted and they would need to readd it to the list.
</panel>

</panel>


