**1 :fas-comment:**
</div>

Also worth noting IntelliJ has the same TODO tool window (View → Tool Windows → TODO), and it picks up FIXME too.


Personally I keep TODOs as comments and save issues for bigger things. Rough line I use is scope: if the fix lives in one file and I'm the one who'll open that file, a comment is enough and it stays next to the code. Issues make more sense when the work spans files or someone else needs to know it exists probably more of a tP thing than an iP one.
</panel>

