### 404. FENG..G YI `@Jigusheng` (1 posts) 
</div>


<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/276" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**1. :fas-info-circle: Request to help with smoke testing JAR file**
</div>

# Help smoke test Lumi v2.0 please

Please help me smoke test the Lumi v1.1 JAR on Windows, macOS, or Linux.

## Preparation

1. Install Java 25.
2. Download `lumi.jar` from the Lumi v2.0 release.
3. Place `lumi.jar` in an empty folder.
4. Open a terminal in that folder.
5. Confirm that Java 25 is being used:

   '''text
   java -version
   '''

6. Launch Lumi:

   '''text
   java -jar "lumi.jar"
   '''

## Links

1. [[Lumi User Guide](https://jigusheng.github.io/ip/)](https://jigusheng.github.io/ip/)
2. [[Lumi v2.0 release](https://github.com/Jigusheng/ip/releases/tag/Lumi-v2.0)](https://github.com/Jigusheng/ip/releases/tag/Lumi-v2.0)

## Test checklist

Please check that:

- The GUI opens without an error.
- The complete Lumi window is displayed correctly.
- The window can be resized and its contents adjust appropriately.
- The following command adds a to-do:

  '''text
  todo Review lecture notes
  '''

- The following command adds a deadline:

  '''text
  deadline Submit project reflection /by 2026-09-30 2359
  '''

- The following command adds an event:

  '''text
  event Team consultation /from 2026-09-28 1400 /to 2026-09-28 1600
  '''

- The following command displays all three tasks:

  '''text
  list
  '''

- The following command marks the first task as completed:

  '''text
  mark 1
  '''

- The following command marks it as incomplete again:

  '''text
  unmark 1
  '''

- The following command finds the matching task:

  '''text
  find lecture
  '''

- The following command reschedules the deadline:

  '''text
  snooze 2 /to 2026-10-02 1800
  '''

- Entering an invalid command such as the following displays a helpful, visually distinct error without closing Lumi or changing the task list:

  '''text
  deadline Submit report /by tomorrow
  '''

- The following command deletes the event:

  '''text
  delete 3
  '''

- Closing and reopening Lumi preserves the remaining tasks, their dates, and their completion statuses.
- The saved data is created inside the empty test folder rather than somewhere else on the computer.
- The following command ends the session and disables further input:

  '''text
  bye
  '''

  Lumi is not currently designed to close its window automatically after `bye`; this is expected.

## Results

Feel free to report the results using this format:

'''yaml
Screenshot of the GUI app
Operating system:
JAR launched successfully: Yes/No
GUI displayed correctly: Yes/No
Checklist items that failed:
Error message, if any:
Additional observations:
'''

If anything fails, please include:

- A screenshot showing the problem.
- The complete error message shown in the terminal.
- The command that caused the problem.
- Whether the problem still occurs after restarting Lumi.

Thank you veryy muchh !
</panel>

</panel>


