### 415. CHAN..RIEL `@HIIMHEY` (1 posts) 
</div>


<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/401#issuecomment-5725293568" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**1 :fas-comment:**
</div>

**Windows smoke test: passed**

- **OS:** Windows 11 25H2 (build 26200.9457)
- **Architecture:** x64
- **Java:** Oracle Java 25.0.1, 64-bit (build 25.0.1+8-LTS-27)
- **Release:** A-Release, `rembot.jar`

The supplied commands were entered one at a time, in the given order, using a separate folder for the test data.

| Check | Result |
| --- | --- |
| Launch using Java 25 with `java -jar rembot.jar` | PASS |
| Add and list all three tasks with the correct descriptions, dates, times, and initial note | PASS |
| `mark 1` marks the todo as done | PASS |
| Add `Include references` to task 2 and find it with `find references` | PASS |
| `on 2026-10-02` finds the project meeting | PASS |
| `deletenote 2` removes task 2's note | PASS |
| `bye` displays a farewell before closing | PASS |
| Restart and run `list` | PASS: all three tasks are restored; task 1 is done, tasks 2 and 3 are not done. Task 1's note remains and task 2's removed note stays removed. |

**Optional malformed-data recovery: PASS**


**What happened**

- RemBot launched with `java -jar rembot.jar` using Java 25. The window showed a welcome message and an empty task list.
- The todo `read book` was added with the note `Borrow from library`. The deadline `submit report` was shown as due on 1 October 2026 at 6:00 PM. The event `project meeting` was shown as running from 2:00 PM to 3:00 PM on 2 October 2026. Running `list` displayed all three tasks.
- After `mark 1`, `read book` showed `[X]`, indicating that it was done. Its note remained attached.
- `note 2 Include references` added the note to `submit report`. Running `find references` returned that task and displayed the note, confirming that the search found text in notes.
- `on 2026-10-02` returned the project meeting with the correct date and time range.
- `deletenote 2` removed the note from `submit report`. The following `list` still showed all three tasks, with task 1 completed and no note on task 2.
- `bye` displayed the farewell message "[Yawn] Need more sleep. Time for bed..." briefly before the window closed.

**After restarting**

Running `list` restored all three tasks. Task 1 was still marked as done, while tasks 2 and 3 were still not done. The dates and times were unchanged. `Borrow from library` was still attached to task 1, and the removed note on task 2 did not return.

**Optional corrupted-data test**

With RemBot closed, the test copy of `data/rem.txt` was replaced with `invalid data`. On the next launch, a dialog reported that the saved task file was damaged and offered **Start Fresh** and **Exit**. The file remained unchanged while the dialog was open.

Choosing **Start Fresh** opened RemBot with an empty task list. Running `list` confirmed there were no tasks. A new empty `data/rem.txt` was created, and the original malformed contents were preserved in `rem-corrupt-20260918-123554.txt`.

**Other observations**

- No functional errors, visible layout problems, or differences from the User Guide were observed during this test sequence.
- JavaFX printed warnings about an unnamed-module configuration and deprecated `sun.misc.Unsafe::allocateMemory` usage. These did not prevent the tested features from working.
- An initial restriction in the automated test environment blocked JavaFX from writing to its native-library cache. After that restriction was resolved, RemBot launched successfully on the normal desktop.
- **Only Windows was tested; macOS and Linux were not tested.**

</panel>

</panel>


