<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/486#issuecomment-5747265594" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**1 :fas-comment:**
</div>

Tested the supplied local slotbot.jar on Windows 11 (build 26200), x64, Eclipse Temurin OpenJDK 25.0.4+7. Copied the JAR into a new empty app folder and launched with `java -jar slotbot.jar`.

## Results

- GUI launched successfully.
- All supplied commands responded without crashing. Creation, listing, search, marking, unmarking, and deletion produced the expected changes.
- Enter and the Send button both submitted commands.
- Unknown commands, missing todo descriptions, invalid task numbers, and invalid dates produced helpful error messages; the session remained usable.
- Leading and trailing spaces around `list` were accepted.
- Resizing and scrolling worked. Messages wrapped and remained readable at the tested smaller window size.
- `bye` closed the first session. After reopening, `list` showed the remaining deadline and event, with their dates and times intact. The deleted todo stayed deleted.

## Commands tested

'''text
todo read chapter 3
deadline submit report /by 2026-09-25
event project meeting /from 2026-09-21 14:00 /to 2026-09-21 15:00
list
find report
reminders
mark 1
unmark 1
delete 1
list
nonsense
todo
mark 99
deadline bad date /by 2026-99-99
  list  
bye
'''

After reopening: `list`, then `bye`.

## Observations and limits

- `reminders` returned the September 25 deadline under “Upcoming reminders (through the next 7 days)” but did not include the September 21 event. This is an observation, not a confirmed defect: the user guide was inaccessible through the web tool, so whether reminders intentionally cover only deadlines could not be verified.
- Startup printed JavaFX/native-access/Unsafe warnings but no fatal startup error.
- No external test report was posted.

## Screenshots

<img width="1000" height="1100" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/33823050-a978-429f-b55c-7bc745671748" />
