### 426. NG W..JIEN `@NGWEIJIEN35` (1 posts) 
</div>


<panel  popup-url="https://github.com/NUS-CS2103-AY2627-S1/forum/issues/233#issuecomment-5684631259" expanded>
<div slot="header">

**1 :fas-comment:**
</div>

Smoke-tested Beemo on Windows

What I tested

- Checked the GUI and resized the window
- Added todos, deadlines, and events
- Tested `list`, `find`, `mark`, `unmark`, and `delete`
- Tested missing descriptions and dates
- Tested an invalid date (`2026-02-30`)
- Tested commands containing repeated spaces
- Closed and reopened the application to confirm that tasks were saved

Most features worked correctly, except one issue:

**Event with an end date earlier than its start date is accepted**

Command: `event training /from 2026-09-16 /to 2026-09-13`

Expected: Beemo should reject the event and explain that the end date cannot be earlier than the start date.

Actual: Beemo added the event successfully

`[E][ ] training (from: 2026-09-16 to: 2026-09-13)`

The invalid event was also shown in the task list and remained after restarting the application.

Apart from this issue, everything I tested worked as expected.

<img width="1913" height="607" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cb2aeff5-4906-498c-8a43-04964cb84ec3" />
<img width="1912" height="1133" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/057cb308-3275-41f9-8cdf-f7c1c3d7dadc" />
